, "location", "ephemeris"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Light travel time correction to the barycentre or heliocentre.\n\nThe frame transformations used to calculate the location of the solar\nsystem barycentre and the heliocentre rely on the erfa routine epv00,\nwhich is consistent with the JPL DE405 ephemeris to an accuracy of\n11.2 km, corresponding to a l", "start_line": 613, "end_line": 692, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sidereal_time", "qualified_name": "sidereal_time", "args": ["self", "kind", "longitude", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate sidereal time.\n\nParameters\n---------------\nkind : str\n    ``'mean'`` or ``'apparent'``, i.e., accounting for precession\n    only, or also for nutation.\nlongitude : `~astropy.units.Quantity`, `str`, or `None`; optional\n    The longitude on the Earth at which to compute the sidereal time.\n  ", "start_line": 694, "end_line": 754, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_erfa_sidereal_time", "qualified_name": "_erfa_sidereal_time", "args": ["self", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate a sidereal time using a IAU precession/nutation model.", "start_line": 761, "end_line": 773, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self", "format"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a fully independent copy the Time object, optionally changing\nthe format.\n\nIf ``format`` is supplied then the time format of the returned Time\nobject will be set accordingly, otherwise it will be unchanged from the\noriginal.\n\nIn this method a full copy of the internal time arrays will be made", "start_line": 775, "end_line": 798, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "replicate", "qualified_name": "replicate", "args": ["self", "format", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a replica of the Time object, optionally changing the format.\n\nIf ``format`` is supplied then the time format of the returned Time\nobject will be set accordingly, otherwise it will be unchanged from the\noriginal.\n\nIf ``copy`` is set to `True` then a full copy of the internal time arrays\nwill ", "start_line": 800, "end_line": 829, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_apply", "qualified_name": "_apply", "args": ["self", "method"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new time object, possibly applying a method to the arrays.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmethod : str or callable\n    If string, can be 'replicate'  or the name of a relevant\n    `~numpy.ndarray` method. In the former case, a new time instance\n    with unchanged internal data is created, while in ", "start_line": 831, "end_line": 924, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__copy__", "qualified_name": "__copy__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overrides the default behavior of the `copy.copy` function in\nthe python stdlib to behave like `Time.copy`. Does *not* make a\ncopy of the JD arrays - only copies by reference.", "start_line": 926, "end_line": 932, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__deepcopy__", "qualified_name": "__deepcopy__", "args": ["self", "memo"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overrides the default behavior of the `copy.deepcopy` function\nin the python stdlib to behave like `Time.copy`. Does make a\ncopy of the JD arrays.", "start_line": 934, "end_line": 940, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_advanced_index", "qualified_name": "_advanced_index", "args": ["self", "indices", "axis", "keepdims"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Turn argmin, argmax output into an advanced index.\n\nArgmin, argmax output contains indices along a given axis in an array\nshaped like the other dimensions.  To use this to get values at the\ncorrect location, a list is constructed in which the other axes are\nindexed sequentially.  For ``keepdims`` is", "start_line": 942, "end_line": 983, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "argmin", "qualified_na