"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1748, "end_line": 1754, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "TimeInfo", "bases": ["MixinInfo"], "methods": ["_represent_as_dict_attrs", "__init__", "unit", "_construct_from_dict_base", "_construct_from_dict"], "docstring": "Container for meta information like name, description, format.  This is\nrequired when the object is used as a mixin column within a table, but can\nbe used as a general way to store meta information.", "start_line": 92, "end_line": 170}, {"name": "TimeDeltaInfo", "bases": ["TimeInfo"], "methods": ["_construct_from_dict"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 173, "end_line": 177}, {"name": "Time", "bases": ["ShapedLikeNDArray"], "methods": ["__new__", "__getnewargs__", "__init__", "_init_from_vals", "_get_time_fmt", "now", "format", "format", "__repr__", "__str__", "scale", "_set_scale", "precision", "precision", "in_subfmt", "in_subfmt", "out_subfmt", "out_subfmt", "shape", "shape", "_shaped_like_input", "jd1", "jd2", "value", "light_travel_time", "sidereal_time", "_erfa_sidereal_time", "copy", "replicate", "_apply", "__copy__", "__deepcopy__", "_advanced_index", "argmin", "argmax", "argsort", "min", "max", "ptp", "sort", "cache", "__getattr__", "__dir__", "_match_shape", "get_delta_ut1_utc", "_get_delta_ut1_utc", "_set_delta_ut1_utc", "_get_delta_tdb_tt", "_set_delta_tdb_tt", "__sub__", "__add__", "__radd__", "__rsub__", "_time_difference", "__lt__", "__le__", "__eq__", "__ne__", "__gt__", "__ge__", "to_datetime"], "docstring": "Represent and manipulate times and dates for astronomy.\n\nA `Time` object is initialized with one or more times in the ``val``\nargument.  The input times in ``val`` must conform to the specified\n``format`` and must correspond to the specified time ``scale``.  The\noptional ``val2`` time input should b", "start_line": 180, "end_line": 1473}, {"name": "TimeDelta", "bases": ["Time"], "methods": ["__init__", "replicate", "_set_scale", "__add__", "__sub__", "__neg__", "__abs__", "__mul__", "__rmul__", "__div__", "__rdiv__", "__truediv__", "__rtruediv__", "to"], "docstring": "Represent the time difference between two times.\n\nA TimeDelta object is initialized with one or more times in the ``val``\nargument.  The input times in ``val`` must conform to the specified\n``format``.  The optional ``val2`` time input should be supplied only for\nnumeric input formats (e.g. JD) wher", "start_line": 1476, "end_line": 1719}, {"name": "ScaleValueError", "bases": ["Exception"], "methods": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1722, "end_line": 1723}, {"name": "OperandTypeError", "bases": ["TypeError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1747, "end_line": 1754}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "The astropy.time package provides functionality for manipulating times and\ndates. Specific emphasis is placed on supporting time scales (e.g. UTC, TAI,\nUT1) and time representations (e.g. JD, MJD, ISO 8601) that are used in\nastronomy.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/cosmology/funcs.py", "file_hash": "2881e90fe7b522f60f3007975a0fbf46ff742c10720202bfeff31211b2dc5b99", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "core", "names": ["CosmologyError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "units", "names": ["Quantity"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.optimize", "names": ["fminbound"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "z_at_value", "qualified_name": "z_at_value", "args": ["func", "fval", "zmin", "zmax", "ztol", "maxfun"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Find the redshift ``z`` at which ``func(z) = fval``.\n\nThis finds the redshift at which one of the cosmology functions or\nmethods (for example Planck13.distmod) is equal to a known value.\n\n.. warning::\n  Make sure you understand the behaviour of the function that you\n  are trying to invert! Depending", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 144, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Convenience functions for `astropy.cosmology`.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/cosmology/__init__.py", "file_hash": "08874872cc35038346f2e60a1763fe703fe73a2724a6c16d5796436c5fd14038", "imports": [{"module": "core", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "funcs", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "astropy.cosmology contains classes and functions for cosmological\ndistance measures and other cosmology-related calculations.\n\nSee the `Astropy documentation\n<http://docs.astropy.org/en/latest/cosmology/index.html>`_ for more\ndetailed usage examples and references.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/cosmology/parameters.py", "file_hash": "1e6b5d7aebdaea118d16b80cbf625f6b0b18bd374f9690988f071c8c99cdfd80", "imports": [], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module contains dictionaries with sets of parameters for a\ngiven cosmology.\n\nEach cosmology has the following parameters defined:\n\n    ==========  =====================================\n    Oc0         Omega cold dark matter at z=0\n    Ob0         Omega baryon at z=0\n    Om0         Omega matter at z=0\n    flat        Is this assumed flat?  If not, Ode0 must be specified\n    Ode0        Omega dark energy at z=0 if flat is False\n    H0          Hubble parameter at z=0 in km/s/Mpc\n    n           Density perturbation spectral index\n    Tcmb0       Current temperature of the CMB\n    Neff        Effective number of neutrino species\n    sigma8      Density perturbation amplitude\n    tau         Ionisation optical depth\n    z_reion     Redshift of hydrogen reionisation\n    t0          Age of the universe in Gyr\n    reference   Reference for the parameters\n    ==========  =====================================\n\nThe list of cosmologies available are given by the tuple\n`available`. Current cosmologies available:\n\nPlanck 2015 (Planck15) parameters from Planck Collaboration 2016, A&A, 594, A13\n (Paper XIII), Table 4 (TT, TE, EE + lowP + lensing + ext)\n\nPlanck 2013 (Planck13) parameters from Planck Collaboration 2014, A&A, 571, A16\n (Paper XVI), Table 5 (Planck + WP + highL + BAO)\n\nWMAP 9 year (WMAP9) parameters from Hinshaw et al. 2013, ApJS, 208, 19,\ndoi: 10.1088/0067-0049/208/2/19. Table 4 (WMAP9 + eCMB + BAO + H0)\n\nWMAP 7 year (WMAP7) parameters from Komatsu et al. 2011, ApJS, 192, 18,\ndoi: 10.1088/0067-0049/192/2/18. Table 1 (WMAP + BAO + H0 ML).\n\nWMAP 5 year (WMAP5) parameters from Komatsu et al. 2009, ApJS, 180, 330,\ndoi: 10.1088/0067-0049/180/2/330. Table 1 (WMAP + BAO + SN ML).", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/cosmology/core.py", "file_hash": "e8620df0c767c63ee1110c008def91ae09aad906f7e78f5369e56cd239237cc3", "imports": [{"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "math", "names": ["sqrt", "pi", "exp", "log", "floor"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "abc", "names": ["ABCMeta", "abstractmethod"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "inspect", "names": ["signature"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "", "names": ["scalar_inv_efuncs"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["constants"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["isiterable"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.state", "names": ["ScienceState"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["parameters"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.integrate", "names": ["quad"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.integrate", "names": ["quad"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.integrate", "names": ["quad"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.integrate", "names": ["quad"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "scipy.integrate", "names": ["quad"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "_float_or_none", "qualified_name": "_float_or_none", "args": ["x", "digits"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper function to format a variable that can be a float or None", "start_line": 2808, "end_line": 2813, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "vectorize_if_needed", "qualified_name": "vectorize_if_needed", "args": ["func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper function to vectorize functions on array inputs", "start_line": 2816, "end_line": 2821, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "H0", "Om0", "Ode0", "Tcmb0", "Neff", "m_nu", "Ob0", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 145, "end_line": 292, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_namelead", "qualified_name": "_namelead", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper function for constructing __repr__", "start_line": 294, "end_line": 300, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 302, "end_line": 308, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "H0", "qualified_name": "H0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the Hubble constant as an `~astropy.units.Quantity` at z=0", "start_line": 314, "end_line": 316, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Om0", "qualified_name": "Om0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega matter; matter density/critical density at z=0", "start_line": 319, "end_line": 321, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ode0", "qualified_name": "Ode0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega dark energy; dark energy density/critical density at z=0", "start_line": 324, "end_line": 326, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ob0", "qualified_name": "Ob0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega baryon; baryonic matter density/critical density at z=0", "start_line": 329, "end_line": 331, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Odm0", "qualified_name": "Odm0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega dark matter; dark matter density/critical density at z=0", "start_line": 334, "end_line": 336, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ok0", "qualified_name": "Ok0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega curvature; the effective curvature density/critical density\nat z=0", "start_line": 339, "end_line": 342, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Tcmb0", "qualified_name": "Tcmb0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Temperature of the CMB as `~astropy.units.Quantity` at z=0", "start_line": 345, "end_line": 347, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Tnu0", "qualified_name": "Tnu0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Temperature of the neutrino background as `~astropy.units.Quantity` at z=0", "start_line": 350, "end_line": 352, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Neff", "qualified_name": "Neff", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Number of effective neutrino species", "start_line": 355, "end_line": 357, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_massive_nu", "qualified_name": "has_massive_nu", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Does this cosmology have at least one massive neutrino species?", "start_line": 360, "end_line": 364, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "m_nu", "qualified_name": "m_nu", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Mass of neutrino species", "start_line": 367, "end_line": 380, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "h", "qualified_name": "h", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Dimensionless Hubble constant: h = H_0 / 100 [km/sec/Mpc]", "start_line": 383, "end_line": 385, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "hubble_time", "qualified_name": "hubble_time", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Hubble time as `~astropy.units.Quantity`", "start_line": 388, "end_line": 390, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "hubble_distance", "qualified_name": "hubble_distance", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Hubble distance as `~astropy.units.Quantity`", "start_line": 393, "end_line": 395, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "critical_density0", "qualified_name": "critical_density0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Critical density as `~astropy.units.Quantity` at z=0", "start_line": 398, "end_line": 400, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ogamma0", "qualified_name": "Ogamma0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega gamma; the density/critical density of photons at z=0", "start_line": 403, "end_line": 405, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Onu0", "qualified_name": "Onu0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Omega nu; the density/critical density of neutrinos at z=0", "start_line": 408, "end_line": 410, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clone", "qualified_name": "clone", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a copy of this object, potentially with some changes.\n\nReturns\n-------\nnewcos : Subclass of FLRW\nA new instance of this class with the specified changes.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThis assumes that the values of all constructor arguments\nare available as properties, which is true of all the provided\nsubc", "start_line": 412, "end_line": 471, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "w", "qualified_name": "w", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": ["abstractmethod"], "docstring": "The dark energy equation of state.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nw : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The dark energy equation of state\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe dark energy equation of state is defined as\n:math:`w(z) = P(z)/\\rho(z)`, where :math:`P(z)` is the\np", "start_line": 474, "end_line": 496, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Om", "qualified_name": "Om", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for non-relativistic matter\nat redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOm : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The density of non-relativistic matter relative to the critical\n  density at each redshift.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThis", "start_line": 498, "end_line": 521, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ob", "qualified_name": "Ob", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for baryonic matter at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOb : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The density of baryonic matter relative to the critical density at\n  each redshift.\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError\n  If Ob", "start_line": 523, "end_line": 547, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Odm", "qualified_name": "Odm", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for dark matter at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOdm : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The density of non-relativistic dark matter relative to the critical\n  density at each redshift.\n\nRaises\n------\nValueErr", "start_line": 549, "end_line": 578, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ok", "qualified_name": "Ok", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the equivalent density parameter for curvature\nat redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOk : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The equivalent density parameter for curvature at each redshift.", "start_line": 580, "end_line": 604, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ode", "qualified_name": "Ode", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for dark energy at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOde : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The density of non-relativistic matter relative to the critical\n  density at each redshift.", "start_line": 606, "end_line": 630, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Ogamma", "qualified_name": "Ogamma", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for photons at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOgamma : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The energy density of photons relative to the critical\n  density at each redshift.", "start_line": 632, "end_line": 649, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Onu", "qualified_name": "Onu", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the density parameter for neutrinos at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nOnu : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The energy density of neutrinos relative to the critical\n  density at each redshift.  Note that this includes their\n  kine", "start_line": 651, "end_line": 677, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Tcmb", "qualified_name": "Tcmb", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the CMB temperature at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nTcmb : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The temperature of the CMB in K.", "start_line": 679, "end_line": 695, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "Tnu", "qualified_name": "Tnu", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the neutrino temperature at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nTnu : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The temperature of the cosmic neutrino background in K.", "start_line": 697, "end_line": 713, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "nu_relative_density", "qualified_name": "nu_relative_density", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Neutrino density function relative to the energy density in\nphotons.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array like\n   Redshift\n\nReturns\n-------\n f : ndarray, or float if z is scalar\n   The neutrino density scaling factor relative to the density\n   in photons at each redshift\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe density in neut", "start_line": 715, "end_line": 783, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_w_integrand", "qualified_name": "_w_integrand", "args": ["self", "ln1pz"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal convenience function for w(z) integral.", "start_line": 785, "end_line": 793, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "de_density_scale", "qualified_name": "de_density_scale", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluates the redshift dependence of the dark energy density.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nI : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The scaling of the energy density of dark energy with redshift.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe scaling factor, I, is defined by :math:`\\rh", "start_line": 795, "end_line": 843, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "efunc", "qualified_name": "efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function used to calculate H(z), the Hubble parameter.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The redshift scaling of the Hubble constant.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe return value, E, is defined such that :math:`H(z) = H_0 E`.\n\nIt is no", "start_line": 845, "end_line": 877, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inv_efunc", "qualified_name": "inv_efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Inverse of efunc.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The redshift scaling of the inverse Hubble constant.", "start_line": 879, "end_line": 904, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_lookback_time_integrand_scalar", "qualified_name": "_lookback_time_integrand_scalar", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Integrand of the lookback time.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : float\n  Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nI : float\n  The integrand for the lookback time\n\nReferences\n----------\nEqn 30 from Hogg 1999.", "start_line": 906, "end_line": 925, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookback_time_integrand", "qualified_name": "lookback_time_integrand", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Integrand of the lookback time.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : float or array-like\n  Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nI : float or array\n  The integrand for the lookback time\n\nReferences\n----------\nEqn 30 from Hogg 1999.", "start_line": 927, "end_line": 950, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_abs_distance_integrand_scalar", "qualified_name": "_abs_distance_integrand_scalar", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Integrand of the absorption distance.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : float\n  Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nX : float\n  The integrand for the absorption distance\n\nReferences\n----------\nSee Hogg 1999 section 11.", "start_line": 952, "end_line": 971, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "abs_distance_integrand", "qualified_name": "abs_distance_integrand", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Integrand of the absorption distance.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : float or array\n  Input redshift.\n\nReturns\n-------\nX : float or array\n  The integrand for the absorption distance\n\nReferences\n----------\nSee Hogg 1999 section 11.", "start_line": 973, "end_line": 995, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "H", "qualified_name": "H", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Hubble parameter (km/s/Mpc) at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nH : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  Hubble parameter at each input redshift.", "start_line": 997, "end_line": 1011, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "scale_factor", "qualified_name": "scale_factor", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Scale factor at redshift ``z``.\n\nThe scale factor is defined as :math:`a = 1 / (1 + z)`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\na : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  Scale factor at each input redshift.", "start_line": 1013, "end_line": 1032, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookback_time", "qualified_name": "lookback_time", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Lookback time in Gyr to redshift ``z``.\n\nThe lookback time is the difference between the age of the\nUniverse now and the age at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar\n\nReturns\n-------\nt : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  Lookback time in Gyr to each", "start_line": 1034, "end_line": 1057, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookback_distance", "qualified_name": "lookback_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The lookback distance is the light travel time distance to a given\nredshift. It is simply c * lookback_time.  It may be used to calculate\nthe proper distance between two redshifts, e.g. for the mean free path\nto ionizing radiation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D", "start_line": 1059, "end_line": 1076, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "age", "qualified_name": "age", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Age of the universe in Gyr at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nt : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The age of the universe in Gyr at each input redshift.\n\nSee Also\n--------\nz_at_value : Find the redshift corresponding to an ", "start_line": 1078, "end_line": 1099, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "critical_density", "qualified_name": "critical_density", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Critical density in grams per cubic cm at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nrho : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  Critical density in g/cm^3 at each input redshift.", "start_line": 1101, "end_line": 1115, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_distance", "qualified_name": "comoving_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance in Mpc at a given\nredshift.\n\nThe comoving distance along the line-of-sight between two\nobjects remains constant with time for objects in the Hubble\nflow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.uni", "start_line": 1117, "end_line": 1136, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving line-of-sight distance in Mpc between objects at\nredshifts z1 and z2.\n\nThe comoving distance along the line-of-sight between two\nobjects remains constant with time for objects in the Hubble\nflow.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : array-like, shape (N,)\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar", "start_line": 1138, "end_line": 1160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_transverse_distance", "qualified_name": "comoving_transverse_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving transverse distance in Mpc at a given redshift.\n\nThis value is the transverse comoving distance at redshift ``z``\ncorresponding to an angular separation of 1 radian. This is\nthe same as the comoving distance if omega_k is zero (as in\nthe current concordance lambda CDM model).\n\nParameters\n--", "start_line": 1162, "end_line": 1186, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_comoving_transverse_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "_comoving_transverse_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving transverse distance in Mpc between two redshifts.\n\nThis value is the transverse comoving distance at redshift\n``z2`` as seen from redshift ``z1`` corresponding to an\nangular separation of 1 radian. This is the same as the\ncomoving distance if omega_k is zero (as in the current\nconcordance l", "start_line": 1188, "end_line": 1223, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "angular_diameter_distance", "qualified_name": "angular_diameter_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular diameter distance in Mpc at a given redshift.\n\nThis gives the proper (sometimes called 'physical') transverse\ndistance corresponding to an angle of 1 radian for an object\nat redshift ``z``.\n\nWeinberg, 1972, pp 421-424; Weedman, 1986, pp 65-67; Peebles,\n1993, pp 325-327.\n\nParameters\n---------", "start_line": 1225, "end_line": 1249, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "luminosity_distance", "qualified_name": "luminosity_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Luminosity distance in Mpc at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is the distance to use when converting between the\nbolometric flux from an object at redshift ``z`` and its\nbolometric luminosity.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.", "start_line": 1251, "end_line": 1280, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "angular_diameter_distance_z1z2", "qualified_name": "angular_diameter_distance_z1z2", "args": ["self", "z1", "z2"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular diameter distance between objects at 2 redshifts.\nUseful for gravitational lensing.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz1, z2 : array-like, shape (N,)\n  Input redshifts. z2 must be large than z1.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.Quantity`, shape (N,) or single if input scalar\n  The angular diameter ", "start_line": 1282, "end_line": 1301, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "absorption_distance", "qualified_name": "absorption_distance", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Absorption distance at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is used to calculate the number of objects with some\ncross section of absorption and number density intersecting a\nsightline per unit redshift path.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : float", "start_line": 1303, "end_line": 1328, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "distmod", "qualified_name": "distmod", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Distance modulus at redshift ``z``.\n\nThe distance modulus is defined as the (apparent magnitude -\nabsolute magnitude) for an object at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\ndistmod : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  Distance modul", "start_line": 1330, "end_line": 1356, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "comoving_volume", "qualified_name": "comoving_volume", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Comoving volume in cubic Mpc at redshift ``z``.\n\nThis is the volume of the universe encompassed by redshifts less\nthan ``z``. For the case of omega_k = 0 it is a sphere of radius\n`comoving_distance` but it is less intuitive\nif omega_k is not 0.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts", "start_line": 1358, "end_line": 1390, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "differential_comoving_volume", "qualified_name": "differential_comoving_volume", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Differential comoving volume at redshift z.\n\nUseful for calculating the effective comoving volume.\nFor example, allows for integration over a comoving volume\nthat has a sensitivity function that changes with redshift.\nThe total comoving volume is given by integrating\ndifferential_comoving_volume to ", "start_line": 1392, "end_line": 1416, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "kpc_comoving_per_arcmin", "qualified_name": "kpc_comoving_per_arcmin", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Separation in transverse comoving kpc corresponding to an\narcminute at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The distance in comoving kpc corresponding to an arcmin at each\n  input redshift.", "start_line": 1418, "end_line": 1434, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "kpc_proper_per_arcmin", "qualified_name": "kpc_proper_per_arcmin", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Separation in transverse proper kpc corresponding to an\narcminute at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\nd : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The distance in proper kpc corresponding to an arcmin at each\n  input redshift.", "start_line": 1436, "end_line": 1452, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "arcsec_per_kpc_comoving", "qualified_name": "arcsec_per_kpc_comoving", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a comoving kpc\nat redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntheta : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a comoving kpc\n  at each input redshi", "start_line": 1454, "end_line": 1470, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "arcsec_per_kpc_proper", "qualified_name": "arcsec_per_kpc_proper", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a proper kpc at\nredshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.  Must be 1D or scalar.\n\nReturns\n-------\ntheta : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n  The angular separation in arcsec corresponding to a proper kpc\n  at each input redshift.", "start_line": 1472, "end_line": 1488, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "H0", "Om0", "Ode0", "Tcmb0", "Neff", "m_nu", "Ob0", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1545, "end_line": 1565, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "w", "qualified_name": "w", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns dark energy equation of state at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nw : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The dark energy equation of state\n\nNotes\n------\nThe dark energy equation of state is defined as\n:math:`w(z) = P(z)/\\rho(z)`, wher", "start_line": 1567, "end_line": 1592, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "de_density_scale", "qualified_name": "de_density_scale", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluates the redshift dependence of the dark energy density.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nI : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The scaling of the energy density of dark energy with redshift.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe scaling factor, I, is defined by :math:`\\rh", "start_line": 1594, "end_line": 1616, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "efunc", "qualified_name": "efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function used to calculate H(z), the Hubble parameter.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The redshift scaling of the Hubble constant.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe return value, E, is defined such that :math:`H(z) = H_0 E`.", "start_line": 1618, "end_line": 1648, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inv_efunc", "qualified_name": "inv_efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function used to calculate :math:`\\frac{1}{H_z}`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The inverse redshift scaling of the Hubble constant.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe return value, E, is defined such that :math:`H_z = H_0 /\nE`.", "start_line": 1650, "end_line": 1678, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "H0", "Om0", "Tcmb0", "Neff", "m_nu", "Ob0", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1730, "end_line": 1753, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "efunc", "qualified_name": "efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function used to calculate H(z), the Hubble parameter.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The redshift scaling of the Hubble constant.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe return value, E, is defined such that :math:`H(z) = H_0 E`.", "start_line": 1755, "end_line": 1785, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inv_efunc", "qualified_name": "inv_efunc", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function used to calculate :math:`\\frac{1}{H_z}`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nE : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The inverse redshift scaling of the Hubble constant.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe return value, E, is defined such that :math:`H_z = H_0 / E`.", "start_line": 1787, "end_line": 1813, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1815, "end_line": 1820, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "H0", "Om0", "Ode0", "w0", "Tcmb0", "Neff", "m_nu", "Ob0", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1883, "end_line": 1906, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "w0", "qualified_name": "w0", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Dark energy equation of state", "start_line": 1909, "end_line": 1911, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "w", "qualified_name": "w", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns dark energy equation of state at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nw : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The dark energy equation of state\n\nNotes\n------\nThe dark energy equation of state is defined as\n:math:`w(z) = P(z)/\\rho(z)`, wher", "start_line": 1913, "end_line": 1938, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "de_density_scale", "qualified_name": "de_density_scale", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluates the redshift dependence of the dark energy density.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-----