se}, {"name": "w", "qualified_name": "w", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns dark energy equation of state at redshift ``z``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nw : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The dark energy equation of state\n\nNotes\n------\nThe dark energy equation of state is defined as\n:math:`w(z) = P(z)/\\rho(z)`, wher", "start_line": 2742, "end_line": 2767, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "de_density_scale", "qualified_name": "de_density_scale", "args": ["self", "z"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluates the redshift dependence of the dark energy density.\n\nParameters\n----------\nz : array-like\n  Input redshifts.\n\nReturns\n-------\nI : ndarray, or float if input scalar\n  The scaling of the energy density of dark energy with redshift.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe scaling factor, I, is defined by :math:`\\\\r", "start_line": 2769, "end_line": 2797, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2799, "end_line": 2805, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_cosmology_from_string", "qualified_name": "get_cosmology_from_string", "args": ["arg"], "decorators": ["staticmethod"], "docstring": "Return a cosmology instance from a string.\n        ", "start_line": 2873, "end_line": 2885, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate", "qualified_name": "validate", "args": ["cls", "value"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2888, "end_line": 2896, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "CosmologyError", "bases": ["Exception"], "methods": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 82, "end_line": 83}, {"name": "Cosmology", "bases": [], "methods": [], "docstring": "Placeholder for when a more general Cosmology class is\nimplemented. ", "start_line": 86, "end_line": 88}, {"name": "FLRW", "bases": ["Cosmology"], "methods": ["__init__", "_namelead", "__repr__", "H0", "Om0", "Ode0", "Ob0", "Odm0", "Ok0", "Tcmb0", "Tnu0", "Neff", "has_massive_nu", "m_nu", "h", "hubble_time", "hubble_distance", "critical_density0", "Ogamma0", "Onu0", "clone", "w", "Om", "Ob", "Odm", "Ok", "Ode", "Ogamma", "Onu", "Tcmb", "Tnu", "nu_relative_density", "_w_integrand", "de_density_scale", "efunc", "inv_efunc", "_lookback_time_integrand_scalar", "lookback_time_integrand", "_abs_distance_integrand_scalar", "abs_distance_integrand", "H", "scale_factor", "lookback_time", "lookback_distance", "age", "critical_density", "comoving_distance", "_comoving_distance_z1z2", "comoving_transverse_distance", "_comoving_transverse_distance_z1z2", "angular_diameter_distance", "luminosity_distance", "angular_diameter_distance_z1z2", "absorption_distance", "distmod", "comoving_volume", "differential_comoving_volume", "kpc_comoving_per_arcmin", "kpc_proper_per_arcmin", "arcsec_per_kpc_comoving", "arcsec_per_kpc_proper"], "docstring": "A class describing an isotropic and homogeneous\n(Friedmann-Lemaitre-Robertson-Walker) cosmology.\n\nThis is an abstract base class -- you can't instantiate\nexamples of this class, but must work with one of its\nsubclasses such as `LambdaCDM` or `wCDM`.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\nH0 : float or scalar `~ast", "start_line": 91, "end_line": 1488}, {"name": "LambdaCDM", "bases": ["FLRW"], "methods": ["__init__", "w", "de_density_scale", "efunc", "inv_efunc"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a cosmological constant and curvature.\n\nThis has no additional attributes beyond those of FLRW.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\nH0 : float or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Hubble constant at z = 0.  If a float, must be in [km/sec/Mpc]\n\nOm0 : float\n    Omega matter: density of non-relativ", "start_line": 1491, "end_line": 1678}, {"name": "FlatLambdaCDM", "bases": ["LambdaCDM"], "methods": ["__init__", "efunc", "inv_efunc", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a cosmological constant and no curvature.\n\nThis has no additional attributes beyond those of FLRW.\n\nParameters\n----------\nH0 : float or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Hubble constant at z = 0.  If a float, must be in [km/sec/Mpc]\n\nOm0 : float\n    Omega matter: density of non-relat", "start_line": 1681, "end_line": 1820}, {"name": "wCDM", "bases": ["FLRW"], "methods": ["__init__", "w0", "w", "de_density_scale", "efunc", "inv_efunc", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a constant dark energy equation of state\nand curvature.\n\nThis has one additional attribute beyond those of FLRW.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\nH0 : float or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Hubble constant at z = 0. If a float, must be in [km/sec/Mpc]\n\nOm0 : float\n    Omega matter: densit", "start_line": 1823, "end_line": 2029}, {"name": "FlatwCDM", "bases": ["wCDM"], "methods": ["__init__", "efunc", "inv_efunc", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a constant dark energy equation of state\nand no spatial curvature.\n\nThis has one additional attribute beyond those of FLRW.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\nH0 : float or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Hubble constant at z = 0. If a float, must be in [km/sec/Mpc]\n\nOm0 : float\n    Omega mat", "start_line": 2032, "end_line": 2180}, {"name": "w0waCDM", "bases": ["FLRW"], "methods": ["__init__", "w0", "wa", "w", "de_density_scale", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a CPL dark energy equation of state and curvature.\n\nThe equation for the dark energy equation of state uses the\nCPL form as described in Chevallier & Polarski Int. J. Mod. Phys.\nD10, 213 (2001) and Linder PRL 90, 91301 (2003):\n:math:`w(z) = w_0 + w_a (1-a) = w_0 + w_a z / (1+z)`.", "start_line": 2183, "end_line": 2348}, {"name": "Flatw0waCDM", "bases": ["w0waCDM"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a CPL dark energy equation of state and no\ncurvature.\n\nThe equation for the dark energy equation of state uses the\nCPL form as described in Chevallier & Polarski Int. J. Mod. Phys.\nD10, 213 (2001) and Linder PRL 90, 91301 (2003):\n:math:`w(z) = w_0 + w_a (1-a) = w_0 + w_a z / (1+z", "start_line": 2351, "end_line": 2447}, {"name": "wpwaCDM", "bases": ["FLRW"], "methods": ["__init__", "wp", "wa", "zp", "w", "de_density_scale", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a CPL dark energy equation of state, a pivot\nredshift, and curvature.\n\nThe equation for the dark energy equation of state uses the\nCPL form as described in Chevallier & Polarski Int. J. Mod. Phys.\nD10, 213 (2001) and Linder PRL 90, 91301 (2003), but modified\nto have a pivot redsh", "start_line": 2450, "end_line": 2635}, {"name": "w0wzCDM", "bases": ["FLRW"], "methods": ["__init__", "w0", "wz", "w", "de_density_scale", "__repr__"], "docstring": "FLRW cosmology with a variable dark energy equation of state\nand curvature.\n\nThe equation for the dark energy equation of state uses the\nsimple form: :math:`w(z) = w_0 + w_z z`.\n\nThis form is not recommended for z > 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\nH0 : float or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Hubble consta", "start_line": 2638, "end_line": 2805}, {"name": "default_cosmology", "bases": ["ScienceState"], "methods": ["get_cosmology_from_string", "validate"], "docstring": "The default cosmology to use.  To change it::\n\n    >>> from astropy.cosmology import default_cosmology, WMAP7\n    >>> with default_cosmology.set(WMAP7):\n    ...     # WMAP7 cosmology in effect\n\nOr, you may use a string::\n\n    >>> with default_cosmology.set('WMAP7'):\n    ...     # WMAP7 cosmology in ", "start_line": 2857, "end_line": 2896}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/tests/pytest_plugins.py", "file_hash": "73cb84d9665a83ab4af90e18393e507d75a9f66c47b2ba17b2ba12d8de22c505", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyDeprecationWarning"], "is_from": true, "a