"Indicates that this parameter is linked to another one.\n\nA callable which provides the relationship of the two parameters.", "start_line": 546, "end_line": 557, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "tied", "qualified_name": "tied", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["tied.setter"], "docstring": "Tie a parameter", "start_line": 560, "end_line": 569, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bounds", "qualified_name": "bounds", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The minimum and maximum values of a parameter as a tuple", "start_line": 572, "end_line": 579, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bounds", "qualified_name": "bounds", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["bounds.setter"], "docstring": "Set the minimum and maximum values of a parameter from a tuple", "start_line": 582, "end_line": 601, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "min", "qualified_name": "min", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A value used as a lower bound when fitting a parameter", "start_line": 604, "end_line": 607, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "min", "qualified_name": "min", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["min.setter"], "docstring": "Set a minimum value of a parameter", "start_line": 610, "end_line": 617, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "max", "qualified_name": "max", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A value used as an upper bound when fitting a parameter", "start_line": 620, "end_line": 623, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "max", "qualified_name": "max", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["max.setter"], "docstring": "Set a maximum value of a parameter.", "start_line": 626, "end_line": 633, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validator", "qualified_name": "validator", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Used as a decorator to set the validator method for a `Parameter`.\nThe validator method validates any value set for that parameter.\nIt takes two arguments--``self``, which refers to the `Model`\ninstance (remember, this is a method defined on a `Model`), and\nthe value being set for this parameter.  T", "start_line": 636, "end_line": 707, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self", "name", "description", "default", "unit", "getter", "setter", "fixed", "tied", "min", "max", "bounds"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make a copy of this `Parameter`, overriding any of its core attributes\nin the process (or an exact copy).\n\nThe arguments to this method are the same as those for the `Parameter`\ninitializer.  This simply returns a new `Parameter` instance with any\nor all of the attributes overridden, and so returns ", "start_line": 709, "end_line": 742, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_raw_value", "qualified_name": "_raw_value", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Currently for internal use only.\n\nLike Parameter.value but does not pass the result through\nParameter.getter.  By design this should only be used from bound\nparameters.\n\nThis will probably be removed are retweaked at some point in the\nprocess of rethinking how parameter values are stored/updated.", "start_line": 745, "end_line": 757, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_bind", "qualified_name": "_bind", "args": ["self", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Bind the `Parameter` to a specific `Model` instance; don't use this\ndirectly on *unbound* parameters, i.e. `Parameter` descriptors that\nare defined in class bodies.", "start_line": 759, "end_line": 768, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_model_value", "qualified_name": "_get_model_value", "args": ["self", "model"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This method implements how to retrieve the value of this parameter from\nthe model instance.  See also `Parameter._set_model_value`.\n\nThese methods take an explicit model argument rather than using\nself._model so that they can be used from unbound `Parameter`\ninstances.", "start_line": 773, "end_line": 799, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_model_value", "qualified_name": "_set_model_value", "args": ["self", "model", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This method implements how to store the value of a parameter on the\nmodel instance.\n\nCurrently there is only one storage mechanism (via the ._parameters\narray) but other mechanisms may be desireable, in which case really the\nmodel class itself should dictate this and *not* `Parameter` itself.", "start_line": 801, "end_line": 827, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_value_wrapper", "qualified_name": "_create_value_wrapper", "args": ["wrapper", "model"], "decorators": ["staticmethod"], "docstring": "Wraps a getter/setter function to support optionally passing in\na reference to the model object as the second argument.\n\nIf a model is tied to this parameter and its getter/setter supports\na second argument then this creates a partial function using the model\ninstance as the second argument.", "start_line": 830, "end_line": 863, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array__", "qualified_name": "__array__", "args": ["self", "dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 865, "end_line": 872, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__bool__", "qualified_name": "__bool__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 874, "end_line": 878, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_parameter_value", "qualified_name": "_update_parameter_value", "args": ["model", "name", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 810, "end_line": 822, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validator", "qualified_name": "validator", "args": ["func", "self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 695, "end_line": 697, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validator", "qualified_name": "validator", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 703, "end_line": 705, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "ParameterError", "bases": ["Exception"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Generic exception class for all exceptions pertaining to Parameters.", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 29}, {"name": "InputParameterError", "bases": ["ValueError", "ParameterError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Used for incorrect input parameter values and definitions.", "start_line": 32, "end_line": 33}, {"name": "ParameterDefinitionError", "bases": ["ParameterError"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Exception in declaration of class-level Parameters.", "start_line": 36, "end_line": 37}, {"name": "Parameter", "bases": ["OrderedDescriptor"], "methods": ["__init__", "__get__", "__set__", "__len__", "__getitem__", "__setitem__", "__repr__", "name", "default", "value", "value", "unit", "unit", "_set_unit", "quantity", "quantity", "shape", "size", "fixed", "fixed", "tied", "tied", "bounds", "bounds", "min", "min", "max", "max", "validator", "copy", "_raw_value", "_bind", "_get_model_value", "_set_model_value", "_create_value_wrapper", "__array__", "__bool__"], "docstring": "Wraps individual parameters.\n\nThis class represents a model's parameter (in a somewhat broad sense).  It\nacts as both a descriptor that can be assigned to a class attribute to\ndescribe the parameters accepted by an individual model (this is called an\n\"unbound parameter\"), or it can act as a proxy fo", "start_line": 131, "end_line": 899}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module defines two classes that deal with parameters.\n\nIt is unlikely users will need to work with these classes directly, unless they\ndefine their own models.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/blackbody.py", "file_hash": "73558dc0c61e202bba1b465f1889770bc3696221fc7f596f9f5e606aa761f68a", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "collections", "names": ["OrderedDict"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "core", "names": ["Fittable1DModel"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "parameters", "names": ["Parameter"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["constants"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "blackbody_nu", "qualified_name": "blackbody_nu", "args": ["in_x", "temperature"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate blackbody flux per steradian, :math:`B_{\\nu}(T)`.\n\n.. note::\n\n    Use `numpy.errstate` to suppress Numpy warnings, if desired.\n\n.. warning::\n\n    Output values might contain ``nan`` and ``inf``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nin_x : number, array-like, or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Frequency, w", "start_line": 249, "end_line": 317, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "blackbody_lambda", "qualified_name": "blackbody_lambda", "args": ["in_x", "temperature"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Like :func:`blackbody_nu` but for :math:`B_{\\lambda}(T)`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nin_x : number, array-like, or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Frequency, wavelength, or wave number.\n    If not a Quantity, it is assumed to be in Angstrom.\n\ntemperature : number, array-like, or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n", "start_line": 320, "end_line": 346, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "evaluate", "qualified_name": "evaluate", "args": ["self", "x", "temperature", "bolometric_flux"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Evaluate the model.\n\nParameters\n----------\nx : float, `~numpy.ndarray`, or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Frequency at which to compute the blackbody. If no units are given,\n    this defaults to Hz.\n\ntemperature : float, `~numpy.ndarray`, or `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Temperature of the blackbody.", "start_line": 182, "end_line": 230, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_units", "qualified_name": "input_units", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 233, "end_line": 237, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parameter_units_for_data_units", "qualified_name": "_parameter_units_for_data_units", "args": ["self", "inputs_unit", "outputs_unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 239, "end_line": 241, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lambda_max", "qualified_name": "lambda_max", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Peak wavelength when the curve is expressed as power density.", "start_line": 244, "end_line": 246, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "BlackBody1D", "bases": ["Fittable1DModel"], "methods": ["evaluate", "input_units", "_parameter_units_for_data_units", "lambda_max"], "docstring": "One dimensional blackbody model.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntemperature : :class:`~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Blackbody temperature.\nbolometric_flux : :class:`~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    The bolometric flux of the blackbody (i.e., the integral over the\n    spectral axis).\n\nNotes\n-----\n\nModel formula:\n", "start_line": 119, "end_line": 246}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Model and functions related to blackbody radiation.\n\n.. _blackbody-planck-law:\n\nBlackbody Radiation\n-------------------\n\nBlackbody flux is calculated with Planck law\n(:ref:`Rybicki & Lightman 1979 <ref-rybicki1979>`):\n\n.. math::\n\n    B_{\\lambda}(T) = \\frac{2 h c^{2} / \\lambda^{5}}{exp(h c / \\lambda k T) - 1}\n\n    B_{\\nu}(T) = \\frac{2 h \\nu^{3} / c^{2}}{exp(h \\nu / k T) - 1}\n\nwhere the unit of :math:`B_{\\lambda}(T)` is\n:math:`erg \\; s^{-1} cm^{-2} \\mathring{A}^{-1} sr^{-1}`, and\n:math:`B_{\\nu}(T)` is :math:`erg \\; s^{-1} cm^{-2} Hz^{-1} sr^{-1}`.\n:func:`~astropy.modeling.blackbody.blackbody_lambda` and\n:func:`~astropy.modeling.blackbody.blackbody_nu` calculate the\nblackbody flux for :math:`B_{\\lambda}(T)` and :math:`B_{\\nu}(T)`,\nrespectively.\n\nFor blackbody representation as a model, see :class:`BlackBody1D`.\n\n.. _blackbody-examples:\n\nExamples\n^^^^^^^^\n\n>>> import numpy as np\n>>> from astropy import units as u\n>>> from astropy.modeling.blackbody import blackbody_lambda, blackbody_nu\n\nCalculate blackbody flux for 5000 K at 100 and 10000 Angstrom while suppressing\nany Numpy warnings:\n\n>>> wavelengths = [100, 10000] * u.AA\n>>> temperature = 5000 * u.K\n>>> with np.errstate(all='ignore'):\n...     flux_lam = blackbody_lambda(wavelengths, temperature)\n...     flux_nu = blackbody_nu(wavelengths, temperature)\n>>> flux_lam  # doctest: +FLOAT_CMP\n<Quantity [  1.27452545e-108,  7.10190526e+005] erg / (Angstrom cm2 s sr)>\n>>> flux_nu  # doctest: +FLOAT_CMP\n<Quantity [  4.25135927e-123,  2.36894060e-005] erg / (cm2 Hz s sr)>\n\nPlot a blackbody spectrum for 5000 K:\n\n.. plot::\n\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    import numpy as np\n    from astropy import constants as const\n    from astropy import units as u\n    from astropy.modeling.blackbody import blackbody_lambda\n\n    temperature = 5000 * u.K\n    wavemax = (const.b_wien / temperature).to(u.AA)  # Wien's displacement law\n    waveset = np.logspace(\n        0, np.log10(wavemax.value + 10 * wavemax.value), num=1000) * u.AA\n    with np.errstate(all='ignore'):\n        flux = blackbody_lambda(waveset, temperature)\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n    ax.plot(waveset.value, flux.value)\n    ax.axvline(wavemax.value, ls='--')\n    ax.get_yaxis().get_major_formatter().set_powerlimits((0, 1))\n    ax.set_xlabel(r'$\\lambda$ ({0})'.format(waveset.unit))\n    ax.set_ylabel(r'$B_{\\lambda}(T)$')\n    ax.set_title('Blackbody, T = {0}'.format(temperature))\n\nNote that an array of temperatures can also be given instead of a single\ntemperature. In this case, the Numpy broadcasting rules apply: for instance, if\nthe frequency and temperature have the same shape, the output will have this\nshape too, while if the frequency is a 2-d array with shape ``(n, m)`` and the\ntemperature is an array with shape ``(m,)``, the output will have a shape\n``(n, m)``.\n\nSee Also\n^^^^^^^^\n\n.. _ref-rybicki1979:\n\nRybicki, G. B., & Lightman, A. P. 1979, Radiative Processes in Astrophysics (New York, NY: Wiley)", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/projections.py", "file_hash": "8b83f267e5e5b97cec3189fb94e17b812c437bfb40f19640f386743785ee735c", "imports": [{"module": "abc", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "core", "names": ["Model"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "parameters", "names": ["Parameter", "InputParameterError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["_projections"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["_to_radian", "_to_orig_unit"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Inverse projection--all projection models must provide an inverse.", "start_line": 113, "end_line": 116, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_units", "qualified_name": "input_units", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 129, "end_line": 130, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "return_units", "qualified_name": "return_units", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 133, "end_line": 134, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "input_units", "qualified_name": "inpu