verse of the current mapping.\n\nRaises\n------\n`NotImplementedError`\n    An inverse does no exist on mappings that drop some of its inputs\n    (there is then no way to reconstruct the inputs that were dropped).", "start_line": 101, "end_line": 123, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "n_inputs", "name", "meta"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 159, "end_line": 161, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 163, "end_line": 167, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The inverse transformation.\n\nIn this case of `Identity`, ``self.inverse is self``.", "start_line": 170, "end_line": 177, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Mapping", "bases": ["FittableModel"], "methods": ["__init__", "inputs", "outputs", "mapping", "__repr__", "evaluate", "inverse"], "docstring": "Allows inputs to be reordered, duplicated or dropped.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmapping : tuple\n    A tuple of integers representing indices of the inputs to this model\n    to return and in what order to return them.  See\n    :ref:`compound-model-mappings` for more details.\nn_inputs : int\n    Number of", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 123}, {"name": "Identity", "bases": ["Mapping"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Returns inputs unchanged.\n\nThis class is useful in compound models when some of the inputs must be\npassed unchanged to the next model.\n\nParameters\n----------\nn_inputs : int\n    Specifies the number of inputs this identity model accepts.\nname : str, optional\n    A human-friendly name associated with ", "start_line": 126, "end_line": 177}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Special models useful for complex compound models where control is needed over\nwhich outputs from a source model are mapped to which inputs of a target model.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/models.py", "file_hash": "cd555bcec03ec1b3b139ade2664745a66c4e4948c7bf9253ebb46d8abe526664", "imports": [{"module": "core", "names": ["custom_model"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "mappings", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "projections", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "rotations", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "polynomial", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "functional_models", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "powerlaws", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "tabular", "names": ["*"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "blackbody", "names": ["BlackBody1D"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Creates a common namespace for all pre-defined models.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/separable.py", "file_hash": "27ae6f39535c3c76b612a745a6d94047f3c6743283f470a17bfc46a28c39e12d", "imports": [{"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "core", "names": ["Model", "_CompoundModel", "ModelDefinitionError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "mappings", "names": ["Mapping"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "is_separable", "qualified_name": "is_separable", "args": ["transform"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A separability test for the outputs of a transform.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntransform : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    A (compound) model.\n\nReturns\n-------\nis_separable : ndarray\n    A boolean array with size ``transform.n_outputs`` where\n    each element indicates whether the output is independe", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 63, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_compute_n_outputs", "qualified_name": "_compute_n_outputs", "args": ["left", "right"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the number of outputs of two models.\n\nThe two models are the left and right model to an operation in\nthe expression tree of a compound model.\n\nParameters\n----------\nleft, right : `astropy.modeling.Model` or ndarray\n    If input is of an array, it is the output of `coord_matrix`.", "start_line": 66, "end_line": 88, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arith_oper", "qualified_name": "_arith_oper", "args": ["left", "right"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function corresponding to one of the arithmetic operators\n['+', '-'. '*', '/', '**'].\n\nThis always returns a nonseparable output.\n\n\nParameters\n----------\nleft, right : `astropy.modeling.Model` or ndarray\n    If input is of an array, it is the output of `coord_matrix`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nresult : ndarr", "start_line": 91, "end_line": 130, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_coord_matrix", "qualified_name": "_coord_matrix", "args": ["model", "pos", "noutp"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create an array representing inputs and outputs of a simple model.\n\nThe array has a shape (noutp, model.n_inputs).\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `astropy.modeling.Model`\n    model\npos : str\n    Position of this model in the expression tree.\n    One of ['left', 'right'].\nnoutp : int\n    Number of ou", "start_line": 133, "end_line": 178, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_cstack", "qualified_name": "_cstack", "args": ["left", "right"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function corresponding to '&' operation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nleft, right : `astropy.modeling.Model` or ndarray\n    If input is of an array, it is the output of `coord_matrix`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nresult : ndarray\n    Result from this operation.", "start_line": 181, "end_line": 209, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_cdot", "qualified_name": "_cdot", "args": ["left", "right"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Function corresponding to \"|\" operation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nleft, right : `astropy.modeling.Model` or ndarray\n    If input is of an array, it is the output of `coord_matrix`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nresult : ndarray\n    Result from this operation.", "start_line": 212, "end_line": 249, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_separable", "qualified_name": "_separable", "args": ["transform"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the separability of outputs.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntransform : `astropy.modeling.Model`\n    A transform (usually a compound model).\n\nReturns\n-------\nis_separable : ndarray of dtype np.bool\n    An array of shape (transform.n_outputs,) of boolean type\n    Each element represents the separab", "start_line": 252, "end_line": 271, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_n_inputs_outputs", "qualified_name": "_n_inputs_outputs", "args": ["input"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 110, "end_line": 115, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_n_inputs_outputs", "qualified_name": "_n_inputs_outputs", "args": ["input", "position"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return ``n_inputs``, ``n_outputs`` for a model or coord_matrix.", "start_line": 229, "end_line": 237, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Functions to determine if a model is separable, i.e.\nif the model outputs are independent.\n\nIt analyzes ``n_inputs``, ``n_outputs`` and the operators\nin a compound model by stepping through the transforms\nand creating a ``coord_matrix`` of shape (``n_outputs``, ``n_inputs``).\n\n\nEach modeling operator is represented by a function which\ntakes two simple models (or two ``coord_matrix`` arrays) and\nreturns an array of shape (``n_outputs``, ``n_inputs``).", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/modeling/fitting.py", "file_hash": "f57b627b9e2642d5a61312e3342