", "qualified_name": "_repr_pretty_", "args": ["cls", "p", "cycle"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Repr for IPython's pretty printer.\n\nBy default IPython \"pretty prints\" classes, so we need to implement\nthis so that IPython displays the custom repr for Models.", "start_line": 135, "end_line": 143, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 145, "end_line": 163, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The name of this model class--equivalent to ``cls.__name__``.\n\nThis attribute is provided for symmetry with the `Model.name` attribute\nof model instances.", "start_line": 166, "end_line": 174, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "n_inputs", "qualified_name": "n_inputs", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 177, "end_line": 178, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "n_outputs", "qualified_name": "n_outputs", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 181, "end_line": 182, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_is_concrete", "qualified_name": "_is_concrete", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A class-level property that determines whether the class is a concrete\nimplementation of a Model--i.e. it is not some abstract base class or\ninternal implementation detail (i.e. begins with '_').", "start_line": 185, "end_line": 191, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "rename", "qualified_name": "rename", "args": ["cls", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Creates a copy of this model class with a new name.\n\nThe new class is technically a subclass of the original class, so that\ninstance and type checks will still work.  For example::\n\n    >>> from astropy.modeling.models import Rotation2D\n    >>> SkyRotation = Rotation2D.rename('SkyRotation')\n    >>> ", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 231, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_inverse_property", "qualified_name": "_create_inverse_property", "args": ["cls", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 233, "end_line": 250, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_bounding_box_property", "qualified_name": "_create_bounding_box_property", "args": ["cls", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Takes any bounding_box defined on a concrete Model subclass (either\nas a fixed tuple or a property or method) and wraps it in the generic\ngetter/setter interface for the bounding_box attribute.", "start_line": 252, "end_line": 291, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_bounding_box_subclass", "qualified_name": "_create_bounding_box_subclass", "args": ["cls", "func", "sig"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "For Models that take optional arguments for defining their bounding\nbox, we create a subclass of _BoundingBox with a ``__call__`` method\nthat supports those additional arguments.\n\nTakes the function's Signature as an argument since that is already\ncomputed in _create_bounding_box_property, so no nee", "start_line": 293, "end_line": 338, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_handle_special_methods", "qualified_name": "_handle_special_methods", "args": ["cls", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 340, "end_line": 415, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_format_cls_repr", "qualified_name": "_format_cls_repr", "args": ["cls", "keywords"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal implementation of ``__repr__``.\n\nThis is separated out for ease of use by subclasses that wish to\noverride the default ``__repr__`` while keeping the same basic\nformatting.", "start_line": 428, "end_line": 477, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self"]