 prefixes)``\ntuple used to format the unit summary docs in `generate_unit_summary`.", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 78, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "generate_unit_summary", "qualified_name": "generate_unit_summary", "args": ["namespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generates a summary of units from a given namespace.  This is used\nto generate the docstring for the modules that define the actual\nunits.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnamespace : dict\n    A namespace containing units.\n\nReturns\n-------\ndocstring : str\n    A docstring containing a summary table of the unit", "start_line": 81, "end_line": 121, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "generate_prefixonly_unit_summary", "qualified_name": "generate_prefixonly_unit_summary", "args": ["namespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generates table entries for units in a namespace that are just prefixes\nwithout the base unit.  Note that this is intended to be used *after*\n`generate_unit_summary` and therefore does not include the table header.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnamespace : dict\n    A namespace containing units that are pre", "start_line": 124, "end_line": 160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_effectively_unity", "qualified_name": "is_effectively_unity", "args": ["value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 163, "end_line": 170, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sanitize_scale", "qualified_name": "sanitize_scale", "args": ["scale"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 173, "end_line": 188, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate_power", "qualified_name": "validate_power", "args": ["p", "support_tuples"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a power to a floating point value, an integer, or a Fraction.\n\nIf a fractional power can be represented exactly as a floating point\nnumber, convert it to a float, to make the math much faster; otherwise,\nretain it as a `fractions.Fraction` object to avoid losing precision.\nConversely, if the", "start_line": 191, "end_line": 242, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "resolve_fractions", "qualified_name": "resolve_fractions", "args": ["a", "b"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If either input is a Fraction, convert the other to a Fraction.\nThis ensures that any operation involving a Fraction will use\nrational arithmetic and preserve precision.", "start_line": 245, "end_line": 257, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "quantity_asanyarray", "qualified_name": "quantity_asanyarray", "args": ["a", "dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 260, "end_line": 265, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Miscellaneous utilities for `astropy.units`.\n\nNone of the functions in the module are meant for use outside of the\npackage.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/physical.py", "file_hash": "b51df8024d38d6753c46210c340641005da690ad54737e6ff6aac55afaff16b0", "imports": [{"module": "", "names": ["core"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["si"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["astrophys"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["cgs"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["imperial"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "def_physical_type", "qualified_name": "def_physical_type", "args": ["unit", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Adds a new physical unit mapping.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : `~astropy.units.UnitBase` instance\n    The unit to map from.\n\nname : str\n    The physical name of the unit.", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 45, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_physical_type", "qualified_name": "get_physical_type", "args": ["unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a unit, returns the name of the physical quantity it\nrepresents.  If it represents an unknown physical quantity,\n``\"unknown\"`` is returned.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : `~astropy.units.UnitBase` instance\n    The unit to lookup\n\nReturns\n-------\nphysical : str\n    The name of the physical quant", "start_line": 48, "end_line": 66, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Defines physical unit names.\n\nThis module is not intended for use by user code directly.  Instead,\nthe physical unit name of a `Unit` can be obtained using its `ptype`\nproperty.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/astrophys.py", "file_hash": "5150bf1925ed74c36f8610b5a7d9248655995468b75889200fcc501e93e0d314", "imports": [{"module": "", "names": ["si"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "constants", "names": ["si"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["UnitBase", "def_unit", "si_prefixes", "binary_prefixes", "set_enabled_units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "_numpy"}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["generate_unit_summary"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This package defines the astrophysics-specific units.  They are also\navailable in the `astropy.units` namespace.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/units/equivalencies.py", "file_hash": "febb638a265541325deab466e2205a6f3648cad2ee7daf6f5a01e0b09964e22d", "imports": [{"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "constants", "names": ["si"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["si"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["cgs"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["astrophys"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "function", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["dimensionless_unscaled"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["UnitsError"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["UnitBase"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "imperial", "names": ["deg_F"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "dimensionless_angles", "qualified_name": "dimensionless_angles", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Allow angles to be equivalent to dimensionless (with 1 rad = 1 m/m = 1).\n\nIt is special compared to other equivalency pairs in that it\nallows this independent of the power to which the angle is raised,\nand independent of whether it is part of a more complicated unit.", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 31, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "logarithmic", "qualified_name": "logarithmic", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Allow logarithmic units to be converted to dimensionless fractions", "start_line": 34, "end_line": 39, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "parallax", "qualified_name": "parallax", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a list of equivalence pairs that handle the conversion\nbetween parallax angle and distance.", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 49, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "spectral", "qualified_name": "spectral", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a list of equivalence pairs that handle spectral\nwavelength, wave number, frequency, and energy equivalences.\n\nAllows conversions between wavelength units, wave number units,\nfrequency units, and energy units as they relate to light.\n\nThere are two types of wave number:\n\n    * spectroscopic ", "start_line": 52, "end_line": 84, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "spectral_density", "qualified_name": "spectral_density", "args": ["wav", "factor"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a list of equivalence pairs that handle spectral density\nwith regard to wavelength and frequency.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwav : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    `~astropy.units.Quantity` associated with values being converted\n    (e.g., wavelength or frequency).\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe ``factor`` argum", "start_line": 87, "end_line": 214, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "doppler_radio", "qualified_name": "doppler_radio", "args": ["rest"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the equivalency pairs for the radio convention for velocity.\n\nThe radio convention for the relation between velocity and frequency is:\n\n:math:`V = c \\frac{f_0 - f}{f_0}  ;  f(V) = f_0 ( 1 - V/c )`\n\nParameters\n----------\nrest : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Any quantity supported by the standa", "start_line": 217, "end_line": 279, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "doppler_optical", "qualified_name": "doppler_optical", "args": ["rest"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the equivalency pairs for the optical convention for velocity.\n\nThe optical convention for the relation between velocity and frequency is:\n\n:math:`V = c \\frac{f_0 - f}{f  }  ;  f(V) = f_0 ( 1 + V/c )^{-1}`\n\nParameters\n----------\nrest : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    Any quantity supported by t", "start_line": 282, "end_line": 345, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "doppler_relativistic", "qualified_name": "doppler_relativistic", "args": ["rest"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the equivalency pairs for the relativistic convention for velocity.\n\nThe full relativistic convention for the relation between velocity and frequency is:\n\n:math:`V = c \\frac{f_0^2 - f^2}{f_0^2 + f^2} ;  f(V) = f_0 \\frac{\\left(1 - (V/c)^2\\right)^{1/2}}{(1+V/c)}`\n\nParameters\n----------\nrest : `", "start_line": 348, "end_line": 418, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "molar_mass_amu", "qualified_name": "molar_mass_amu", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the equivalence between amu and molar mass.", "start_line": 421, "end_line": 427, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "mass_energy", "qualified_name": "mass_energy", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a list of equivalence pairs that handle the conversion\nbetween mass and energy.", "start_line": 430, "end_line": 446, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "brightness_temperature", "qualified_name": "brightness_temperature", "args": ["beam_area", "disp"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Defines the conversion between Jy/beam and \"brightness temperature\",\n:math:`T_B`, in Kelvins.  The brightness temperature is a unit very\ncommonly used in radio astronomy.  See, e.g., \"Tools of Radio Astronomy\"\n(Wilson 2009) eqn 8.16 and eqn 8.19 (these pages are available on `google\nbooks\n<http://bo", "start_line": 449, "end_line": 508, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "temperature", "qualified_name": "temperature", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert between Kelvin, Celsius, and Fahrenheit here because\nUnit and CompositeUnit cannot do addition or subtraction properly.", "start_line": 511, "end_line": 520, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "temperature_energy", "qualified_name": "temperature_energy", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert between Kelvin and keV(eV) to an equivalent amount.", "start_line": 523, "end_line": 527, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assert_is_spectral_unit", "qualified_name": "assert_is_spectral_unit", "args": ["value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 530, "end_line": 535, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pixel_scale", "qualified_name": "pixel_scale", "args": ["pixscale"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert between pixel distances (in units of ``pix``) and angular units,\ngiven a particular ``pixscale``.\n\nParameters\n----------\npixscale : `~astropy.units.Quantity`\n    The pixel scale either in units of angle/pixel or pixel/angle.", "start_line": 538, "end_line": 556, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "plate_scale", "qualified_name": "plate_scale", "args": ["platescale"], "d