ueError if an equivalency cannot be interpreted", "start_line": 62, "end_line": 101, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_current_unit_registry", "qualified_name": "get_current_unit_registry", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 279, "end_line": 280, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_enabled_units", "qualified_name": "set_enabled_units", "args": ["units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Sets the units enabled in the unit registry.\n\nThese units are searched when using\n`UnitBase.find_equivalent_units`, for example.\n\nThis may be used either permanently, or as a context manager using\nthe ``with`` statement (see example below).\n\nParameters\n----------\nunits : list of sequences, dicts, or", "start_line": 283, "end_line": 332, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_enabled_units", "qualified_name": "add_enabled_units", "args": ["units"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Adds to the set of units enabled in the unit registry.\n\nThese units are searched when using\n`UnitBase.find_equivalent_units`, for example.\n\nThis may be used either permanently, or as a context manager using\nthe ``with`` statement (see example below).\n\nParameters\n----------\nunits : list of sequences,", "start_line": 335, "end_line": 387, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_enabled_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "set_enabled_equivalencies", "args": ["equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Sets the equivalencies enabled in the unit registry.\n\nThese equivalencies are used if no explicit equivalencies are given,\nboth in unit conversion and in finding equivalent units.\n\nThis is meant in particular for allowing angles to be dimensionless.\nUse with care.\n\nParameters\n----------\nequivalencie", "start_line": 390, "end_line": 423, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_enabled_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "add_enabled_equivalencies", "args": ["equivalencies"], "dec