ent to `other`.\nSee `is_equivalent`, except that a proper Unit object should be\ngiven (i.e., no string) and that the equivalency list should be\nnormalized using `_normalize_equivalencies`.", "start_line": 791, "end_line": 820, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_apply_equivalencies", "qualified_name": "_apply_equivalencies", "args": ["self", "unit", "other", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Internal function (used from `_get_converter`) to apply\nequivalence pairs.", "start_line": 822, "end_line": 869, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_converter", "qualified_name": "_get_converter", "args": ["self", "other", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 871, "end_line": 899, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_to", "qualified_name": "_to", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the scale to the specified unit.\n\nSee `to`, except that a Unit object should be given (i.e., no\nstring), and that all defaults are used, i.e., no\nequivalencies and value=1.", "start_line": 901, "end_line": 932, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to", "qualified_name": "to", "args": ["self", "other", "value", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the converted values in the specified unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nother : unit object or string\n    The unit to convert to.\n\nvalue : scalar int or float, or sequence convertible to array, optional\n    Value(s) in the current unit to be converted to the\n    specified unit.  If not provided, d", "start_line": 934, "end_line": 965, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "in_units", "qualified_name": "in_units", "args": ["self", "other", "value", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Alias for `to` for backward compatibility with pynbody.", "start_line": 967, "end_line": 972, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "decompose", "qualified_name": "decompose", "