ppress printing the unit\nin each row since it is already at the top in the ", "start_line": 122, "end_line": 133, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_construct_from_dict", "qualified_name": "_construct_from_dict", "args": ["self", "map"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 144, "end_line": 148, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "new_like", "qualified_name": "new_like", "args": ["self", "cols", "length", "metadata_conflicts", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a new Quantity instance which is consistent with the\ninput ``cols`` and has ``length`` rows.\n\nThis is intended for creating an empty column object whose elements can\nbe set in-place for table operations like join or vstack.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncols : list\n    List of input columns\nlength :", "start_line": 150, "end_line": 196, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__new__", "qualified_name": "__new__", "args": ["cls", "value", "unit", "dtype", "copy", "order", "subok", "ndmin"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 273, "end_line": 391, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_finalize__", "qualified_name": "__array_finalize__", "args": ["self", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 393, "end_line": 405, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_prepare__", "qualified_name": "__array_prepare__", "args": ["self", "obj", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 407, "end_line": 503, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_wrap__", "qualified_name": "__array_wrap__", "args": ["self", "obj", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 505, "end_line": 591, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_ufunc__", "qualified_name": "__array_ufunc__", "args": ["self", "function", "method"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrap numpy ufuncs, taking care of units.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfunction : callable\n    ufunc to wrap.\nmethod : str\n    Ufunc method: ``__call__``, ``at``, ``reduce``, etc.\ninputs : tuple\n    Input arrays.\nkwargs : keyword arguments\n    As passed on, with ``out`` containing possible quantity output.", "start_line": 593, "end_line": 644, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_result_as_quantity", "qualified_name": "_result_as_quantity", "args": ["self", "result", "unit", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Turn result into a quantity with the given unit.\n\nIf no output is given, it will take a view of the array as a quantity,\nand set the unit.  If output is given, those should be quantity views\nof the result arrays, and the function will just set the unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nresult : `~numpy.ndarra", "start_line": 646, "end_line": 684, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__quantity_subclass__", "qualified_name": "__quantity_subclass__", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Overridden by subclasses to change what kind of view is\ncreated based on the output unit of an operation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : UnitBase\n    The unit for which the appropriate class should be returned\n\nReturns\n-------\ntuple :\n    - `Quantity` subclass\n    - bool: True if subclasses of the gi", "start_line": 686, "end_line": 702, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_new_view", "qualified_name": "_new_view", "args": ["self", "obj", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a Quantity view of some array-like input, and set the unit\n\nBy default, return a view of ``obj`` of the same class as ``self`` and\nwith the same unit.  Subclasses can override the type of class for a\ngiven unit using ``__quantity_subclass__``, and can ensure properties\nother than the unit are", "start_line": 704, "end_line": 759, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_unit", "qualified_name": "_set_unit", "args": ["self", "unit"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the unit.\n\nThis is used anywhere the unit is set or modified, i.e., in the\ninitilizer, in ``__imul__`` and ``__itruediv__`` for in-place\nmultiplication and division by another unit, as well as in\n``__array_finalize__`` for wrapping up views.  For Quantity, it just\nsets the unit, but subclasses c", "start_line": 761, "end_line": 780, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__deepcopy__", "qualified_name": "__deepcopy__", "args": ["self", "memo"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 782, "end_line": 785, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 787, "end_line": 793, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setstate__", "qualified_name": "__setstate__", "args": ["self", "state"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 795, "end_line": 801, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_to_value", "qualified_name": "_to_value", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for to and to_value.", "start_line": 805, "end_line": 810, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to", "qualified_name": "to", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a new `~astropy.units.Quantity` object with the specified unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : `~astropy.units.UnitBase` instance, str\n    An object that represents the unit to convert to. Must be\n    an `~astropy.units.UnitBase` object or a string parseable\n    by the `~astropy.units` package", "start_line": 812, "end_line": 838, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_value", "qualified_name": "to_value", "args": ["self", "unit", "equivalencies"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The numerical value, possibly in a different unit.\n\nParameters\n----------\nunit : `~astropy.units.UnitBase` instance or str, optional\n    The unit in which the value should be given. If not given or `None`,\n    use the current unit.\n\nequivalencies : list of equivalence pairs, optional\n    A list of e", "start_line": 840, "end_line": 873, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit", "qualified_name": "unit", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A `~astropy.units.UnitBase` object representing the unit of this\nquantity.", "start_line": 884, "end_line": 890, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "equivalencies", "qualified_name": "equivalencies", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A list of equivalencies that will be applied by default during\nunit conversions.", "start_line": 893, "end_line": 899, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "si", "qualified_name": "si", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns a copy of the current `Quantity` instance with SI units. The\nvalue of the resulting object will be scaled.", "start_line": 902, "end_line": 909, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "cgs", "qualified_name": "cgs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns a copy of the current `Quantity` instance with CGS units. The\nvalue of the resulting object will be scaled.", "start_line": 912, "end_line": 919, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "isscalar", "qualified_name": "isscalar", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "True if the `value` of this quantity is a scalar, or False if it\nis an array-like object.\n\n.. note::\n    This is subtly different from `numpy.isscalar` in that\n    `numpy.isscalar` returns False for a zero-dimensional array\n    (e.g. ``np.array(1)``), while this is True for quantities,\n    since qua", "start_line": 922, "end_line": 933, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__dir__", "qualified_name": "__dir__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["override__dir__"], "docstring": "Quantities are able to directly convert to other units that\nhave t