figuration file for the root\npackage of the requested package/module.\n\nThis overwrites any changes that may have been made in `ConfigItem`\nobjects.  This applies for any items that are based on this file, which\nis determined by the *root* package of ``package", "start_line": 552, "end_line": 571, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_unedited_config_file", "qualified_name": "is_unedited_config_file", "args": ["content", "template_content"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines if a config file can be safely replaced because it doesn't\nactually contain any meaningful content.\n\nTo meet this criteria, the config file must be either:\n\n- All comments or completely empty\n\n- An exact match to a \"legacy\" version of the config file prior to\n  Astropy 0.4, when APE3 was ", "start_line": 574, "end_line": 620, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_default_config", "qualified_name": "update_default_config", "args": ["pkg", "default_cfg_dir_or_fn", "version"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Checks if the configuration file for the specified package exists,\nand if not, copy over the default configuration.  If the\nconfiguration file looks like it has already been edited, we do\nnot write over it, but instead write a file alongside it named\n``pkg.version.cfg`` as a \"template\" for the user.", "start_line": 624, "end_line": 719, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["cls", "name", "bases", "dict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 68, "end_line": 74, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_temp", "qualified_name": "set_temp", "args": ["self", "attr", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Temporarily set a configuration value.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str\n    Configuration item name\n\nvalue : object\n    The value to set temporarily.\n\nExamples\n--------\n>>> import astropy\n>>> with astropy.conf.set_temp('use_color', False):\n...     pass\n...     # console output will not contain colo", "start_line": 95, "end_line": 117, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload", "qualified_name": "reload", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reload a configuration item from the configuration file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str, optional\n    The name of the configuration parameter to reload.  If not\n    provided, reload all configuration parameters.", "start_line": 119, "end_line": 136, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reset", "qualified_name": "reset", "args": ["self", "attr"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reset a configuration item to its default.\n\nParameters\n----------\nattr : str, optional\n    The name of the configuration parameter to reload.  If not\n    provided, reset all configuration parameters.", "start_line": 138, "end_line": 157, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "defaultvalue", "description", "cfgtype", "module", "aliases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 220, "end_line": 265, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "obj", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 267, "end_line": 268, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__get__", "qualified_name": "__get__", "args": ["self", "obj", "objtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 270, "end_line": 273, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set", "qualified_name": "set", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Sets the current value of this ``ConfigItem``.\n\nThis also updates the comments that give the description and type\ninformation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nvalue\n    The value this item should be set to.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If the provided ``value`` is not valid for this ``ConfigItem``.", "start_line": 275, "end_line": 300, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_temp", "qualified_name": "set_temp", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": ["contextmanager"], "docstring": "Sets this item to a specified value only inside a with block.\n\nUse as::\n\n    ITEM = ConfigItem('ITEM', 'default', 'description')\n\n    with ITEM.set_temp('newval'):\n        #... do something that wants ITEM's value to be 'newval' ...\n        print(ITEM)\n\n    # ITEM is now 'default' after the with blo", "start_line": 303, "end_line": 328, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reload", "qualified_name": "reload", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Reloads the value of this ``ConfigItem`` from the relevant\nconfiguration file.\n\nReturns\n-------\nval\n    The new value loaded from the configuration file.", "start_line": 330, "end_line": 356, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__repr__", "qualified_name": "__repr__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 358, "end_line": 361, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__str__", "qualified_name": "__str__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 363, "end_line": 373, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the value of this ``ConfigItem``\n\nReturns\n-------\nval\n    This item's value, with a type determined by the ``cfgtype``\n    attribute.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If the configuration value as stored is not this item's type.", "start_line": 375, "end_line": 440, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_validate_val", "qualified_name": "_validate_val", "args": ["self", "val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Validates the provided value based on cfgtype and returns the\ntype-cast value\n\nthrows the underlying configobj exception if it fails", "start_line": 442, "end_line": 451, "is_async": false, "is_me