art_line": 129, "end_line": 220, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "vstack", "qualified_name": "vstack", "args": ["tables", "join_type", "metadata_conflicts"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Stack tables vertically (along rows)\n\nA ``join_type`` of 'exact' means that the tables must all have exactly\nthe same column names (though the order can vary).  If ``join_type``\nis 'inner' then the intersection of common columns will be the output.\nA value of 'outer' (default) means the output will ", "start_line": 223, "end_line": 286, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "hstack", "qualified_name": "hstack", "args": ["tables", "join_type", "uniq_col_name", "table_names", "metadata_conflicts"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Stack tables along columns (horizontally)\n\nA ``join_type`` of 'exact' means that the tables must all\nhave exactly the same number of rows.  If ``join_type`` is 'inner' then\nthe intersection of rows will be the output.  A value of 'outer' (default)\nmeans the output will have the union of all rows, wi", "start_line": 289, "end_line": 357, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unique", "qualified_name": "unique", "args": ["input_table", "keys", "silent", "keep"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the unique rows of a table.\n\nParameters\n----------\n\ninput_table : `~astropy.table.Table` object or a value that\n    will initialize a `~astropy.table.Table` object\nkeys : str or list of str\n    Name(s) of column(s) used to create unique rows.\n    Default is to use all columns.\nkeep : one of ", "start_line": 360, "end_line": 488, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_col_name_map", "qualified_name": "get_col_name_map", "args": ["arrays", "common_names", "uniq_col_name", "table_names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Find the column names mapping when merging the list of tables\n``arrays``.  It is assumed that col names in ``common_names`` are to be\nmerged into a single column while the