, "docstring": "", "start_line": 322, "end_line": 326, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "aggregate", "qualified_name": "aggregate", "args": ["self", "func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Aggregate each group in the Table into a single row by applying the reduction\nfunction ``func`` to group values in each column.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfunc : function\n    Function that reduces an array of values to a single value\n\nReturns\n-------\nout : Table\n    New table with the aggregated rows.", "start_line": 328, "end_line": 361, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "filter", "qualified_name": "filter", "args": ["self", "func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Filter groups in the Table based on evaluating function ``func`` on each\ngroup sub-table.\n\nThe function which is passed to this method must accept two arguments:\n\n- ``table`` : `Table` object\n- ``key_colnames`` : tuple of column names in ``table`` used as keys for grouping\n\nIt must then return eithe", "start_line": 363, "end_line": 398, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "keys", "qualified_name": "keys", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 401, "end_line": 402, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "BaseGroups", "bases": [], "methods": ["parent", "__iter__", "next", "__getitem__", "__repr__", "__len__"], "docstring": "A class to represent groups within a table of heterogeneous data.\n\n  - ``keys``: key values corresponding to each group\n  - ``indices``: index values in parent table or column corresponding to group boundaries\n  - ``aggregate()``: method to create new table by aggregating within groups", "start_line": 154, "end_line": 208}, {"name": "ColumnGroups", "bases": ["BaseGroups"], "methods": ["__init__", "indices", "keys", "aggregate", "filter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 211, "end_line": 300}, {"name": "TableGroups", "bases": ["BaseGroups"], "methods": ["__init__", "key_colnames"