ss of the value for ``copy_data``.", "start_line": 2546, "end_line": 2563, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__deepcopy__", "qualified_name": "__deepcopy__", "args": ["self", "memo"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2565, "end_line": 2566, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__copy__", "qualified_name": "__copy__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2568, "end_line": 2569, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__lt__", "qualified_name": "__lt__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2571, "end_line": 2572, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__gt__", "qualified_name": "__gt__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2574, "end_line": 2575, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__le__", "qualified_name": "__le__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2577, "end_line": 2578, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__ge__", "qualified_name": "__ge__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2580, "end_line": 2581, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__eq__", "qualified_name": "__eq__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2583, "end_line": 2605, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__ne__", "qualified_name": "__ne__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2607, "end_line": 2608, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "groups", "qualified_name": "groups", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2611, "end_line": 2614, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "group_by", "qualified_name": "group_by", "args": ["self", "keys"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Group this table by the specified ``keys``\n\nThis effectively splits the table into groups which correspond to\nunique values of the ``keys`` grouping object.  The output is a new\n`TableGroups` which contains a copy of this table but sorted by row\naccording to ``keys``.\n\nThe ``keys`` input to `group_b", "start_line": 2616, "end_line": 2644, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "to_pandas", "qualified_name": "to_pandas", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a :class:`pandas.DataFrame` instance\n\nReturns\n-------\ndataframe : :class:`pandas.DataFrame`\n    A pandas :class:`pandas.DataFrame` instance\n\nRaises\n------\nImportError\n    If pandas is not installed\nValueError\n    If the Table contains mixin or multi-dimensional columns", "start_line": 2646, "end_line": 2686, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "from_pandas", "qualified_name": "from_pandas", "args": ["cls", "dataframe"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Create a `Table` from a :class:`pandas.DataFrame` instance\n\nParameters\n----------\ndataframe : :class:`pandas.DataFrame`\n    The pandas :class:`pandas.DataFrame` instance\n\nReturns\n-------\ntable : `Table`\n    A `Table` (or subclass) instance", "start_line": 2689, "end_line": 2730, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_add_as_mixin_column", "qualified_name": "_add_as_mixin_column", "args": ["self", "col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determine if ``col`` should be added to the table directly as\na mixin column.", "start_line": 2768, "end_line": 2773, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_col_for_table", "qualified_name": "_convert_col_for_table", "args": ["self", "col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2775, "end_line": 2786, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__new__", "qualified_name": "__new__", "args": ["cls", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2797, "end_line": 2801, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_finalize__", "qualified_name": "__array_finalize__",