_", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "contrast", "bias"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 504, "end_line": 507, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__call__", "qualified_name": "__call__", "args": ["self", "values", "clip", "out"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 509, "end_line": 520, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "inverse", "qualified_name": "inverse", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A stretch object that performs the inverse operation.", "start_line": 523, "end_line": 525, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "BaseStretch", "bases": ["BaseTransform"], "methods": ["__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Base class for the stretch classes, which, when called with an array\nof values in the range [0:1], return an transformed array of values,\nalso in the range [0:1].", "start_line": 47, "end_line": 78}, {"name": "LinearStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A linear stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = x", "start_line": 81, "end_line": 97}, {"name": "SqrtStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A square root stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\sqrt{x}", "start_line": 100, "end_line": 118}, {"name": "PowerStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A power stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = x^a\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float\n    The power index (see the above formula).", "start_line": 121, "end_line": 148}, {"name": "PowerDistStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "An alternative power stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{a^x - 1}{a - 1}\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float, optional\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  Default is 1000.\n    ``a`` cannot be set to 1.", "start_line": 151, "end_line": 183}, {"name": "InvertedPowerDistStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Inverse transformation for\n`~astropy.image.scaling.PowerDistStretch`.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{\\log(y (a-1) + 1)}{\\log a}\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float, optional\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  Default is 1000.\n    ``a`` cannot be set to 1.", "start_line": 186, "end_line": 219}, {"name": "SquaredStretch", "bases": ["PowerStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A convenience class for a power stretch of 2.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = x^2", "start_line": 222, "end_line": 238}, {"name": "LogStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A log stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{\\log{(a x + 1)}}{\\log{(a + 1)}}.\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  Default is 1000.", "start_line": 241, "end_line": 271}, {"name": "InvertedLogStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Inverse transformation for `~astropy.image.scaling.LogStretch`.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{e^{y} (a + 1) -1}{a}\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float, optional\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  Default is 1000.", "start_line": 274, "end_line": 304}, {"name": "AsinhStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "An asinh stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{{\\rm asinh}(x / a)}{{\\rm asinh}(1 / a)}.\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float, optional\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  The value of\n    this parameter is where the asinh curve transitions from linear\n    to logarit", "start_line": 307, "end_line": 340}, {"name": "SinhStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A sinh stretch.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = \\frac{{\\rm sinh}(x / a)}{{\\rm sinh}(1 / a)}\n\nParameters\n----------\na : float, optional\n    The ``a`` parameter used in the above formula.  Default is 1/3.", "start_line": 343, "end_line": 372}, {"name": "HistEqStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A histogram equalization stretch.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata : array-like\n    The data defining the equalization.\nvalues : array-like, optional\n    The input image values, which should already be normalized to\n    the [0:1] range.", "start_line": 375, "end_line": 410}, {"name": "InvertedHistEqStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Inverse transformation for `~astropy.image.scaling.HistEqStretch`.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata : array-like\n    The data defining the equalization.\nvalues : array-like, optional\n    The input image values, which should already be normalized to\n    the [0:1] range.", "start_line": 413, "end_line": 441}, {"name": "ContrastBiasStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "A stretch that takes into account contrast and bias.\n\nThe stretch is given by:\n\n.. math::\n    y = (x - {\\rm bias}) * {\\rm contrast} + 0.5\n\nand the output values are clipped to the [0:1] range.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncontrast : float\n    The contrast parameter (see the above formula).\n\nbias : float\n ", "start_line": 444, "end_line": 486}, {"name": "InvertedContrastBiasStretch", "bases": ["BaseStretch"], "methods": ["__init__", "__call__", "inverse"], "docstring": "Inverse transformation for ContrastBiasStretch.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncontrast : float\n    The contrast parameter (see\n    `~astro