": [], "docstring": "Used to raise a consistent exception for any operation that is not\nsupported when a representation has differentials attached.", "start_line": 544, "end_line": 552, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_compatible_differentials", "qualified_name": "_compatible_differentials", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 555, "end_line": 556, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "differentials", "qualified_name": "differentials", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A dictionary of differential class instances.\n\nThe keys of this dictionary must be a string representation of the SI\nunit with which the differential (derivative) is taken. For example, for\na velocity differential on a positional representation, the key would be\n``'s'`` for seconds, indicating that ", "start_line": 559, "end_line": 568, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unit_vectors", "qualified_name": "unit_vectors", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Cartesian unit vectors in the direction of each component.\n\nGiven unit vectors :math:`\\hat{e}_c` and scale factors :math:`f_c`,\na change in one component of :math:`\\delta c` corresponds to a change\nin representation of :math:`\\delta c \\times f_c \\times \\hat{e}_c`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nunit_vectors : dic", "start_line": 573, "end_line": 586, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "scale_factors", "qualified_name": "scale_factors", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Scale factors for each component's direction.\n\nGiven unit vectors :math:`\\hat{e}_c` and scale factors :math:`f_c`,\na change in one component of :math:`\\delta c` corresponds to a change\nin representation of :math:`\\delta c \\times f_c \\times \\hat{e}_c`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nscale_factors : dict of `~astro", "start_line": 588, "end_line": 601, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_re_represent_differentials"