 kernel is the difference between two Tophat kernels of\ndifferent width. This kernel is useful for, e.g., background estimation.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius_in : number\n    Inner radius of the ring kernel.\nwidth : number\n    Width of the ring kernel.\nmode : s", "start_line": 363, "end_line": 420}, {"name": "Trapezoid1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "1D trapezoid kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwidth : number\n    Width of the filter kernel, defined as the width of the constant part,\n    before it begins to slope down.\nslope : number\n    Slope of the filter kernel's tails\nmode : str, optional\n    One of the following discretization modes:\n        ", "start_line": 423, "end_line": 478}, {"name": "TrapezoidDisk2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D trapezoid kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius : number\n    Width of the filter kernel, defined as the width of the constant part,\n    before it begins to slope down.\nslope : number\n    Slope of the filter kernel's tails\nmode : str, optional\n    One of the following discretization modes:\n       ", "start_line": 481, "end_line": 538}, {"name": "MexicanHat1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "1D Mexican hat filter kernel.\n\nThe Mexican Hat, or inverted Gaussian-Laplace filter, is a\nbandpass filter. It smoothes the data and removes slowly varying\nor constant structures (e.g. Background). It is useful for peak or\nmulti-scale detection.\n\nThis kernel is derived from a normalized Gaussian func", "start_line": 541, "end_line": 608}, {"name": "MexicanHat2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Mexican hat filter kernel.\n\nThe Mexican Hat, or inverted Gaussian-Laplace filter, is a\nbandpass filter. It smoothes the data and removes slowly varying\nor constant structures (e.g. Background). It is useful for peak or\nmulti-scale detection.\n\nThis kernel is derived from a normalized Gaussian func", "start_line": 611, "end_line": 681}, {"name": "AiryDisk2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Airy disk kernel.\n\nThis kernel models the diffraction pattern of a circular aperture. This\nkernel is normalized to a peak value of 1.\n\nParameters\n----------\nradius : float\n    The radius of the Airy disk kernel (radius of the first zero).\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the ", "start_line": 684, "end_line": 744}, {"name": "Moffat2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "2D Moffat kernel.\n\nThis kernel is a typical model for a seeing limited PSF.\n\nParameters\n----------\ngamma : float\n    Core width of the Moffat model.\nalpha : float\n    Power index of the Moffat model.\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = 8 * radius.\ny_size", "start_line": 747, "end_line": 810}, {"name": "Model1DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel1D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Create kernel from 1D model.\n\nThe model has to be centered on x = 0.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.Fittable1DModel`\n    Kernel response function model\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = 8 * width.\nmode : str, optional\n    One of the ", "start_line": 813, "end_line": 874}, {"name": "Model2DKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Create kernel from 2D model.\n\nThe model has to be centered on x = 0 and y = 0.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.Fittable2DModel`\n    Kernel response function model\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = 8 * width.\ny_size : odd int, optional", "start_line": 877, "end_line": 942}, {"name": "PSFKernel", "bases": ["Kernel2D"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Initialize filter kernel from astropy PSF instance.", "start_line": 945, "end_line": 952}, {"name": "CustomKernel", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__", "array", "array"], "docstring": "Create filter kernel from list or array.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : list or array\n    Filter kernel array. Size must be odd.\n\nRaises\n------\nTypeError\n    If array is not a list or array.\nKernelSizeError\n    If array size is even.\n\nSee also\n--------\nModel2DKernel, Model1DKernel\n\nExamples\n--------", "start_line": 955, "end_line": 1026}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/convolution/core.py", "file_hash": "87efd49eba4cf3a4f5823185d5e70b68f94d11280045d0afe22210543af9b45f", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "copy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["discretize_model", "add_kernel_arrays_1D", "add_kernel_arrays_2D"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "kernel_arithmetics", "qualified_name": "kernel_arithmetics", "args": ["kernel", "value", "operation"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add, subtract or multiply two kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nkernel : `astropy.convolution.Kernel`\n    Kernel instance\nvalue : kernel, float or int\n    Value to operate with\noperation : {'add', 'sub', 'mul'}\n    One of the following operations:\n        * 'add'\n            Add two kernels\n        * ", "start_line": 315, "end_line": 370, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 44, "end_line": 45, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "truncation", "qualified_name": "truncation", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Deviation from the normalization to one.", "start_line": 48, "end_line": 52, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_bool", "qualified_name": "is_bool", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Indicates if kernel is bool.\n\nIf the kernel is bool the multiplication in the convolution could\nbe omitted, to increase the performance.", "start_line": 55, "end_line": 62, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "model", "qualified_name": "model", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Kernel response model.", "start_line": 65, "end_line": 69, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dimension", "qualified_name": "dimension", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Kernel dimension.", "start_line": 72, "end_line": 76, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "center", "qualified_name": "center", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Index of the kernel center.", "start_line": 79, "end_line": 83, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "normalize", "qualified_name": "normalize", "args": ["self", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Normalize the filter kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmode : {'integral', 'peak'}\n    One of the following modes:\n        * 'integral' (default)\n            Kernel is normalized such that its integral = 1.\n        * 'peak'\n            Kernel is normalized such that its peak = 1.", "start_line": 85, "end_line": 113, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Shape of the kernel array.", "start_line": 116, "end_line": 120, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "separable", "qualified_name": "separable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Indicates if the filter kernel is separable.\n\nA 2D filter is separable, when its filter array can be written as the\nouter product of two 1D arrays.\n\nIf a filter kernel is separable, higher dimension convolutions will be\nperformed by applying the 1D filter array consecutively on every dimension.\nThis", "start_line": 123, "end_line": 135, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "array", "qualified_name": "array", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Filter kernel array.", "start_line": 138, "end_line": 142, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__add__", "qualified_name": "__add__", "args": ["self", "kernel"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add two filter kernels.", "start_line": 144, "end_line": 148, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__sub__", "qualified_name": "__sub__", "args": ["self", "kernel"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Subtract two filter kernels.", "start_line": 150, "end_line": 154, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__mul__", "qualified_name": "__mul__", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Multiply kernel with number or convolve two kernels.", "start_line": 156, "end_line": 160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__rmul__", "qualified_name": "__rmul__", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Multiply kernel with number or convolve two kernels.", "start_line": 162, "end_line": 166, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array__", "qualified_name": "__array__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Array representation of the kernel.", "start_line": 168, "end_line": 172, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_wrap__", "qualified_name": "__array_wrap__", "args": ["self", "array", "context"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrapper for multiplication with numpy arrays.", "start_line": 174, "end_line": 181, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "model", "x_size", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 216, "end_line": 240, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "model", "x_size", "y_size", "array"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 277, "end_line": 312, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Kernel", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "truncation", "is_bool", "model", "dimension", "center", "normalize", "shape", "separable", "array", "__add__", "__sub__", "__mul__", "__rmul__", "__array__", "__array_wrap__"], "docstring": "Convolution kernel base class.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : `~numpy.ndarray`\n    Kernel array.", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 181}, {"name": "Kernel1D", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Base class for 1D filter kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.FittableModel`\n    Model to be evaluated.\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size of the kernel array. Default = 8 * width.\narray : `~numpy.ndarray`\n    Kernel array.\nwidth : number\n    Width of the filter kernel.\nmode :", "start_line": 184, "end_line": 240}, {"name": "Kernel2D", "bases": ["Kernel"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Base class for 2D filter kernels.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.FittableModel`\n    Model to be evaluated.\nx_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in x direction of the kernel array. Default = 8 * width.\ny_size : odd int, optional\n    Size in y direction of the kernel array. Default =", "start_line": 243, "end_line": 312}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This module contains the convolution and filter functionalities of astropy.\n\nA few conceptual notes:\nA filter kernel is mainly characterized by its response function. In the 1D\ncase we speak of \"impulse response function\", in the 2D case we call it \"point\nspread function\". This response function is given for every kernel by an\nastropy `FittableModel`, which is evaluated on a grid to obtain a filter array,\nwhich can then be applied to binned data.\n\nThe model is centered on the array and should have an amplitude such that the array\nintegrates to one per default.\n\nCurrently only symmetric 2D kernels are supported.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/convolution/convolve.py", "file_hash": "059ce09c5082e32b5adab14aa24b7c5d340c4c10786f6cff296235dfd0bf85bc", "imports": [{"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "functools", "names": ["partial"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "core", "names": ["Kernel", "Kernel1D", "Kernel2D", "MAX_NORMALIZATION"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.console", "names": ["human_file_size"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.decorators", "names": ["deprecated_renamed_argument"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "nddata", "names": ["support_nddata"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "modeling.core", "names": ["_make_arithmetic_operator", "BINARY_OPERATORS"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "modeling.core", "names": ["_CompoundModelMeta"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "boundary_none", "names": ["convolve1d_boundary_none", "convolve2d_boundary_none", "convolve3d_boundary_none"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "boundary_extend", "names": ["convolve1d_boundary_extend", "convolve2d_boundary_extend", "convolve3d_boundary_extend"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "boundary_fill", "names": ["convolve1d_boundary_fill", "convolve2d_boundary_fill", "convolve3d_boundary_fill"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "boundary_wrap", "names": ["convolve1d_boundary_wrap", "convolve2d_boundary_wrap", "convolve3d_boundary_wrap"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "convolve", "qualified_name": "convolve", "args": ["array", "kernel", "boundary", "fill_value", "nan_treatment", "normalize_kernel", "mask", "preserve_nan", "normalization_zero_tol"], "decorators": ["support_nddata(data='array')"], "docstring": "Convolve an array with a kernel.\n\nThis routine differs from `scipy.ndimage.convolve` because\nit includes a special treatment for ``NaN`` values. Rather than\nincluding ``NaN`` values in the array in the convolution calculation, which\ncauses large ``NaN`` holes in the convolved array, ``NaN`` values a", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 312, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve_fft", "qualified_name": "convolve_fft", "args": ["array", "kernel", "boundary", "fill_value", "nan_treatment", "normalize_kernel", "normalization_zero_tol", "preserve_nan", "mask", "crop", "return_fft", "fft_pad", "psf_pad", "quiet", "min_wt", "allow_huge", "fftn", "ifftn", "complex_dtype"], "decorators": ["deprecated_renamed_argument('interpolate_nan', 'nan_treatment', 'v2.0.0')", "support_nddata(data='array')"], "docstring": "Convolve an ndarray with an nd-kernel.  Returns a convolved image with\n``shape = array.shape``.  Assumes kernel is centered.\n\n`convolve_fft` is very similar to `convolve` in that it replaces ``NaN``\nvalues in the original image with interpolated values using the kernel as\nan interpolation function. ", "start_line": 317, "end_line": 740, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "interpolate_replace_nans", "qualified_name": "interpolate_replace_nans", "args": ["array", "kernel", "convolve"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a data set containing NaNs, replace the NaNs by interpolating from\nneighboring data points with a given kernel.\n\nParameters\n----------\narray : `numpy.ndarray`\n    Array to be convolved with ``kernel``.  It can be of any\n    dimensionality, though only 1, 2, and 3d arrays have been tested.\nkern", "start_line": 743, "end_line": 781, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convolve_models", "qualified_name": "convolve_models", "args": ["model", "kernel", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convolve two models using `~astropy.convolution.convolve_fft`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nmodel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Functional model\nkernel : `~astropy.modeling.core.Model`\n    Convolution kernel\nmode : str\n    Keyword representing which function to use for convolution.\n        * 'convo", "start_line": 784, "end_line": 815, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/__init__.py", "file_hash": "a968b26d0a0e06991f74d359255af0ac35715ce2d2a152ce4cbe0de5fd4c0c5c", "imports": [], "functions": [], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "This subpackage contains modules and packages for interpreting data storage\nformats used by and in astropy.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/registry.py", "file_hash": "bf383b69fb5909eae9f85c94ca9dcbd806eb788739329ddf3adf42bcfe45cb05", "imports": [{"module": "contextlib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "pathlib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "re", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "collections", "names": ["OrderedDict"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "operator", "names": ["itemgetter"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "table", "names": ["Table"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.data", "names": ["get_readable_fileobj"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "delay_doc_updates", "qualified_name": "delay_doc_updates", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["contextlib.contextmanager"], "docstring": "Contextmanager to disable documentation updates when registering\nreader and writer. The documentation is only built once when the\ncontextmanager exits.\n\n.. versionadded:: 1.3\n\nParameters\n----------\ncls : class\n    Class for which the documentation updates should be delayed.\n\nNotes\n-----\nRegistering ", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 75, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_formats", "qualified_name": "get_formats", "args": ["data_class", "readwrite"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the list of registered I/O formats as a Table.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_class : classobj, optional\n    Filter readers/writer to match data class (default = all classes).\n\nreadwrite : str or None, optional\n    Search only for readers (``\"Read\"``) or writers (``\"Write\"``). If None\n    search fo", "start_line": 78, "end_line": 143, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update__doc__", "qualified_name": "_update__doc__", "args": ["data_class", "readwrite"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the docstring to include all the available readers / writers for the\n``data_class.read`` or ``data_class.write`` functions (respectively).", "start_line": 146, "end_line": 202, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "register_reader", "qualified_name": "register_reader", "args": ["data_format", "data_class", "function", "force"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Register a reader function.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier. This is the string that will be used to\n    specify the data type when reading.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that the reader produces.\nfunction : function\n    The function to rea", "start_line": 205, "end_line": 231, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unregister_reader", "qualified_name": "unregister_reader", "args": ["data_format", "data_class"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Unregister a reader function\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that the reader produces.", "start_line": 234, "end_line": 253, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "register_writer", "qualified_name": "register_writer", "args": ["data_format", "data_class", "function", "force"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Register a table writer function.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier. This is the string that will be used to\n    specify the data type when writing.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that can be written.\nfunction : function\n    The function to wr", "start_line": 256, "end_line": 282, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unregister_writer", "qualified_name": "unregister_writer", "args": ["data_format", "data_class"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Unregister a writer function\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that can be written.", "start_line": 285, "end_line": 304, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "register_identifier", "qualified_name": "register_identifier", "args": ["data_format", "data_class", "identifier", "force"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Associate an identifier function with a specific data type.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier. This is the string that is used to\n    specify the data type when reading/writing.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that can be written.\nidentifier : ", "start_line": 307, "end_line": 357, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "unregister_identifier", "qualified_name": "unregister_identifier", "args": ["data_format", "data_class"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Unregister an identifier function\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_format : str\n    The data format identifier.\ndata_class : classobj\n    The class of the object that can be read/written.", "start_line": 360, "end_line": 376, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "identify_format", "qualified_name": "identify_forma