locations for the package and\nprovides a local filename for the data.\n\nThis function is similar to `get_pkg_data_fileobj` but returns the\nfile *name* instead of a readable file-like object.  This means\nthat this function must always cache remote files locally,", "start_line": 466, "end_line": 593, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_pkg_data_contents", "qualified_name": "get_pkg_data_contents", "args": ["data_name", "package", "encoding", "cache"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Retrieves a data file from the standard locations and returns its\ncontents as a bytes object.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata_name : str\n    Name/location of the desired data file.  One of the following:\n\n        * The name of a data file included in the source\n          distribution.  The path is relat", "start_line": 596, "end_line": 669, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_pkg_data_filenames", "qualified_name": "get_pkg_data_filenames", "args": ["datadir", "package", "pattern"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the path of all of the data files in a given directory\nthat match a given glob pattern.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndatadir : str\n    Name/location of the desired data files.  One of the following:\n\n        * The name of a directory included in the source\n          distribution.  The path is rela", "start_line": 672, "end_line": 726, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_pkg_data_fileobjs", "qualified_name": "get_pkg_data_fileobjs", "args": ["datadir", "package", "pattern", "encoding"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns readable file objects for all of the data files in a given\ndirectory that match a given glob pattern.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndatadir : str\n    Name/location of the desired data files.  One of the following:\n\n        * The name of a directory included in the source\n          distribution.  Th", "start_line": 729, "end_line": 790, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "compute_hash", "qualified_name": "compute_hash", "args": ["localfn"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Computes the MD5 hash for a file.\n\nThe hash for a data file is used for looking up data files in a unique\nfashion. This is of particular use for tests; a test may require a\nparticular version of a particular file, in which case it can be accessed\nvia hash to get the appropriate version.\n\nTypically, ", "start_line": 793, "end_line": 827, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_find_pkg_data_path", "qualified_name": "_find_pkg_data_path", "args": ["data_name", "package"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Look for data in the source-included data directories and return the\npath.", "start_line": 830, "end_line": 867, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_find_hash_fn", "qualified_name": "_find_hash_fn", "args": ["hash"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Looks for a local file by hash - returns file name if found and a valid\nfile, otherwise returns None.", "start_line": 870, "end_line": 886, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_free_space_in_dir", "qualified_name": "get_free_space_in_dir", "args": ["path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a path to a directory, returns the amount of free space (in\nbytes) on that filesystem.\n\nParameters\n----------\npath : str\n    The path to a directory\n\nReturns\n-------\nbytes : int\n    The amount of free space on the partition that the directory\n    is on.", "start_line": 889, "end_line": 917, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_free_space_in_dir", "qualified_name": "check_free_space_in_dir", "args": ["path", "size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines if a given directory has enough space to hold a file of\na given size.  Raises an OSError if the file would be too large.\n\nParameters\n----------\npath : str\n    The path to a directory\n\nsize : int\n    A proposed filesize (in bytes)\n\nRaises\n-------\nOSError : There is not enough room on the f", "start_line": 920, "end_line": 944, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "download_file", "qualified_name": "download_file", "args": ["remote_url", "cache", "show_progress", "timeout"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Accepts a URL, downloads and optionally caches the result\nreturning the filename, with a name determined by the file's MD5\nhash. If ``cache=True`` and the file is present in the cache, just\nreturns the filename.\n\nParameters\n----------\nremote_url : str\n    The URL of the file to download\n\ncache : boo", "start_line": 947, "end_line": 1082, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_url_in_cache", "qualified_name": "is_url_in_cache", "args": ["url_key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check if a download from ``url_key`` is in the cache.\n\nParameters\n----------\nurl_key : string\n    The URL retrieved\n\nReturns\n-------\nin_cache : bool\n    `True` if a download from ``url_key`` is in the cache", "start_line": 1085, "end_line": 1111, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_do_download_files_in_parallel", "qualified_name": "_do_download_files_in_parallel", "args": ["args"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1114, "end_line": 1115, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "download_files_in_parallel", "qualified_name": "download_files_in_parallel", "args": ["urls", "cache", "show_progress", "timeout"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Downloads multiple files in parallel from the given URLs.  Blocks until\nall files have downloaded.  The result is a list of local file paths\ncorresponding to the given urls.\n\nParameters\n----------\nurls : list of str\n    The URLs to retrieve.\n\ncache : bool, optional\n    Whether to use the cache (defa", "start_line": 1118, "end_line": 1181, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_deltemps", "qualified_name": "_deltemps", "args": [], "decorators": ["atexit.register"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1190, "end_line": 1198, "is_async": fa