assmethod`.\n\nThe wrapped method may explicitly use the `classmethod` decorator (which\nmust become before this decorator), or the `classmethod` may be omitted\n(it is implicit through use of this d", "start_line": 496, "end_line": 660}, {"name": "lazyproperty", "bases": ["property"], "methods": ["__init__", "__get__", "__set__", "__delete__"], "docstring": "Works similarly to property(), but computes the value only once.\n\nThis essentially memorizes the value of the property by storing the result\nof its computation in the ``__dict__`` of the object instance.  This is\nuseful for computing the value of some property that should otherwise be\ninvariant.  Fo", "start_line": 663, "end_line": 731}, {"name": "sharedmethod", "bases": ["classmethod"], "methods": ["__get__", "_make_method"], "docstring": "This is a method decorator that allows both an instancemethod and a\n`classmethod` to share the same name.\n\nWhen using `sharedmethod` on a method defined in a class's body, it\nmay be called on an instance, or on a class.  In the former case it\nbehaves like a normal instance method (a reference to the", "start_line": 734, "end_line": 798}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "Sundry function and class decorators.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/utils/data_info.py", "file_hash": "659133687499762bbd6380dd38c0603518b927c1959a00cb9bab05e7e2d4d538", "imports": [{"module": "os", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "re", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "weakref", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "io", "names": ["StringIO"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "copy", "names": ["deepcopy"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "functools", "names": ["partial"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "collections", "names": ["OrderedDict"], "is_from": true,