er, returns a signal name.  If the signal\nnumber is unknown, returns ``'UNKNOWN'``.", "start_line": 283, "end_line": 294, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_path_hidden", "qualified_name": "is_path_hidden", "args": ["filepath"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines if a given file or directory is hidden.\n\nParameters\n----------\nfilepath : str\n    The path to a file or directory\n\nReturns\n-------\nhidden : bool\n    Returns `True` if the file is hidden", "start_line": 319, "end_line": 338, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "walk_skip_hidden", "qualified_name": "walk_skip_hidden", "args": ["top", "onerror", "followlinks"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A wrapper for `os.walk` that skips hidden files and directories.\n\nThis function does not have the parameter ``topdown`` from\n`os.walk`: the directories must always be recursed top-down when\nusing this function.\n\nSee also\n--------\nos.walk : For a description of the parameters", "start_line": 341, "end_line": 360, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "strip_accents", "qualified_name": "strip_accents", "args": ["s"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove accents from a Unicode string.\n\nThis helps with matching \"\u00e5ngstr\u00f6m\" to \"angstrom\", for example.", "start_line": 408, "end_line": 416, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "did_you_mean", "qualified_name": "did_you_mean", "args": ["s", "candidates", "n", "cutoff", "fix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "When a string isn't found in a set of candidates, we can be nice\nto provide a list of alternatives in the exception.  This\nconvenience function helps to format that part of the exception.\n\nParameters\n----------\ns : str\n\ncandidates : sequence of str or dict of str keys\n\nn : int\n    The maximum number", "start_line": 419, "end_line": 494, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_locale", "qualified_name": "set_locale", "args": ["name"], "decorators": ["contextmanager"], "docstring": "Context manager to temporarily set the locale to ``name``.\n\nAn example is setting locale to \"C\" so that the C strtod()\nfunction will use \".\" as the decimal point to enable consistent\nnumerical string parsing.\n\nNote that one cannot nest multiple set_locale() context manager\nstatements as this causes ", "start_line": 830, "end_line": 860, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_broadcast", "qualified_name": "check_broadcast", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Determines whether two or more Numpy arrays can be broadcast with each\nother based on their shape tuple alone.\n\nParameters\n----------\n*shapes : tuple\n    All shapes to include in the comparison.  If only one shape is given it\n    is passed through unmodified.  If no shapes are given returns an empty", "start_line": 1062, "end_line": 1107, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dtype_bytes_or_chars", "qualified_name": "dtype_bytes_or_chars", "args": ["dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parse the number out of a dtype.str value like '<U5' or '<f8'.\n\nSee #5819 for discussion on the need for this function for getting\nthe number of characters corresponding to a string dtype.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndtype : numpy dtype object\n    Input dtype\n\nReturns\n-------\nbytes_or_chars : int or None", "start_line": 1110, "end_line": 1129, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name": "write", "args": ["self", "s"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 63, "end_line": 64, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "seed"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 146, "end_line": 147, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__enter__", "qualified_name": "__enter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 149, "end_line": 153, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__exit__",