": "Defined for convenient sorting of `OrderedDescriptor` instances, which\nare defined to sort in their creation order.", "start_line": 608, "end_line": 624, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["cls", "cls_name", "bases", "members"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 763, "end_line": 823, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property", "abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "The shape of the instance and underlying arrays.", "start_line": 892, "end_line": 893, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_apply", "qualified_name": "_apply", "args": ["method"], "decorators": ["abc.abstractmethod"], "docstring": "Create a new instance, with ``method`` applied to underlying data.\n\nThe method is any of the shape-changing methods for `~numpy.ndarray`\n(``reshape``, ``swapaxes``, etc.), as well as those picking particular\nelements (``__getitem__``, ``take``, etc.). It will be applied to the\nunderlying arrays (e.g", "start_line": 896, "end_line": 914, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ndim", "qualified_name": "ndim", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The number of dimensions of the instance and underlying arrays.", "start_line": 917, "end_line": 919, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "size", "qualified_name": "size", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The size of the object, as calculated from its shape.", "start_line": 922, "end_line": 927, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "isscalar", "qualified_name": "isscalar", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 930, "end_line": 931, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__len__", "qualified_name": "__len__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 933, "end_line": 937, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__bool__", "qualified_name": "__bool__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Any instance should evaluate to True, except when it is empty.", "start_line": 939, "end_line": 941, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 943, "end_line": 951, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 953, "end_line": 965, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance containing copies of the internal data.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.copy`.", "start_line": 967, "end_line": 972, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "reshape", "qualified_name": "reshape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns an instance containing the same data with a new shape.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.reshape`.  Note that it is\nnot always possible to change the shape of an array without copying the\ndata (see :func:`~numpy.reshape` documentation). If you want an error\nto be raise if the data", "start_line": 974, "end_line": 984, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ravel", "qualified_name": "ravel", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance with the array collapsed into one dimension.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.ravel`. Note that it is\nnot always possible to unravel an array without copying the data.\nIf you want an error to be raise if the data is copied, you should\nshould assign shape ``(-1,)`` to t", "start_line": 986, "end_line": 994, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "flatten", "qualified_name": "flatten", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a copy with the array collapsed into one dimension.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.flatten`.", "start_line": 996, "end_line": 1001, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "transpose", "qualified_name": "transpose", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance with the data transposed.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.transpose`.  All internal\ndata are views of the data of the original.", "start_line": 1003, "end_line": 1009, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "T", "qualified_name": "T", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return an instance with the data transposed.\n\nParameters are as for :attr:`~numpy.ndarray.T`.  All internal\ndata are views of the data of the original.", "start_line": 1012, "end_line": 1021, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "swapaxes", "qualified_name": "swapaxes", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance with the given axes interchanged.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.swapaxes`:\n``axis1, axis2``.  All internal data are views of the data of the\noriginal.", "start_line": 1023, "end_line": 1030, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "diagonal", "qualified_name": "diagonal", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance with the specified diagonals.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.diagonal`.  All internal\ndata are views of the data of the original.", "start_line": 1032, "end_line": 1038, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "squeeze", "qualified_name": "squeeze", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an instance with single-dimensional shape entries removed\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.squeeze`.  All internal\ndata are views of the data of the original.", "start_line": 1040, "end_line": 1046, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "take", "qualified_name": "take", "args": ["self", "indices", "axis", "mode"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a new instance formed from the elements at the given indices.\n\nParameters are as for :meth:`~numpy.ndarray.take`, except that,\nobviously, no output array can be given.", "start_line": 1048, "end_line": 1054, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "shape_a", "shape_a_idx", "shape_b", "shape_b_idx"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1058, "end_line": 1059, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_public_member", "qualified_name": "is_public_member", "args": ["key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 524, "end_line": 528, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "self_iter", "qualified_name": "self_iter", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 961, "end_line": 963, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "_DummyFile", "bases": [], "methods": ["write"], "docstring": "A noop writeable object.", "start_line": 60, "end_line": 64}, {"name": "NumpyRNGContext", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__enter__", "__exit__"], "docstring": "A context manager (for use with the ``with`` statement) that will seed the\nnumpy random number generator (RNG) to a specific value, and then restore\nthe RNG state back to whatever it was before.\n\nThis is primarily intended for use in the astropy testing suit, but it\nmay be useful in ensuring reprodu", "start_line": 114, "end_line": 158}, {"name": "JsonCustomEncoder", "bases": ["json.JSONEncoder"], "methods": ["default"], "docstring": "Support for data types that JSON default encoder\ndoes not do.\n\nThis includes:\n\n    * Numpy array or number\n    * Complex number\n    * Set\n    * Bytes\n    * astropy.UnitBase\n    * astropy.Quantity\n\nExamples\n--------\n>>> import json\n>>> import numpy as np\n>>> from astropy.utils.misc import JsonCustomE", "start_line": 363, "end_line": 405}, {"name": "InheritDocstrings", "bases": ["type"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "This metaclass makes methods of a class automatically have their\ndocstrings filled in from the methods they override in the base\nclass.\n\nIf the class uses multiple inheritance, the docstring will be\nchosen from the first class in the bases list, in the same way as\nmethods are normally resolved in Py", "start_line": 497, "end_line": 540}, {"name": "OrderedDescriptor", "bases": [], "methods": ["_class_attribute_", "__init__", "__lt__"], "docstring": "Base class for descriptors whose order in the class body should be\npreserved.  Intended for use in concert with the\n`OrderedDescriptorContainer` metaclass.\n\nSubclasses of `OrderedDescriptor` must define a value for a class attribute\ncalled ``_class_attribute_``.  This is the name of a class attribut", "start_line": 543, "end_line": 624}, {"name": "OrderedDescriptorContainer", "bases": ["type"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "Classes should use this metaclass if they wish to use `OrderedDescriptor`\nattributes, which are class attributes that \"remember\" the order in which\nthey were defined in the class body.\n\nEvery subclass of `OrderedDescriptor` has an attribute called\n``_class_attribute_``.  For example, if we have\n\n.. ", "start_line": 627, "end_line": 823}, {"name": "ShapedLikeNDArray", "bases": [], "methods": ["shape", "_apply", "ndim", "size", "isscalar", "__len__", "__bool__", "__getitem__", "__iter__", "copy", "reshape", "ravel", "flatten", "transpose", "T", "swapaxes", "diagonal", "squeeze", "take"], "docstring": "Mixin class to provide shape-changing methods.\n\nThe class proper is assumed to have some underlying data, which are arrays\nor array-like structures. It must define a ``shape`` property, which gives\nthe shape of those data, as well as an ``_apply`` method that creates a new\ninstance in which a `~nump", "start_line": 863, "end_line": 1054}, {"name": "IncompatibleShapeError", "bases": ["ValueError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "do