 "test_slicing_on_class", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test slicing a simple compound model class using integers.", "start_line": 303, "end_line": 356, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing_on_instance", "qualified_name": "test_slicing_on_instance", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test slicing a simple compound model class using integers.", "start_line": 359, "end_line": 398, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_indexing_on_instance", "qualified_name": "test_indexing_on_instance", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test indexing on compound model instances.", "start_line": 401, "end_line": 453, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_basic_compound_inverse", "qualified_name": "test_basic_compound_inverse", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test basic inversion of compound models in the limited sense supported for\nmodels made from compositions and joins only.", "start_line": 456, "end_line": 463, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_compound_unsupported_inverse", "qualified_name": "test_compound_unsupported_inverse", "args": ["model"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.parametrize('model', [Shift(0) + Shift(0) | Shift(0), Shift(0) - Shift(0) | Shift(0), Shift(0) * Shift(0) | Shift(0), Shift(0) / Shift(0) | Shift(0), Shift(0) ** Shift(0) | Shift(0), Gaussian1D(1, 2, 3) | Gaussian1D(4, 5, 6)])"], "docstring": "Ensure inverses aren't supported in cases where it shouldn't be.", "start_line": 473, "end_line": 479, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_mapping_basic_permutations", "qualified_name": "test_mapping_basic_permutations", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests a couple basic examples of the Mapping model--specifically examples\nthat merely permute the outputs.", "start_line": 482, "end_line": 502, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_mapping_inverse", "qualified_name": "test_mapping_inverse", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests inverting a compound model that includes a `Mapping`.", "start_line": 505, "end_line": 517, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_identity_input", "qualified_name": "test_identity_input", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test a case where an Identity (or Mapping) model is the first in a chain\nof composite models and thus is responsible for handling input broadcasting\nproperly.\n\nRegression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/pull/3362", "start_line": 520, "end_line": 538, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing_on_instances_2", "qualified_name": "test_slicing_on_instances_2", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "More slicing tests.\n\nRegression test for https://github.com/embray/astropy/pull/10", "start_line": 541, "end_line": 578, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing_on_instances_3", "qualified_name": "test_slicing_on_instances_3", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Like `test_slicing_on_instances_2` but uses a compound model that does not\nhave any invalid slices due to the resulting model being invalid\n(originally test_slicing_on_instances_2 passed without any\nModelDefinitionErrors being raised, but that was before we prevented\ninvalid models from being create", "start_line": 581, "end_line": 609, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing_on_instance_with_parameterless_model", "qualified_name": "test_slicing_on_instance_with_parameterless_model", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test to fix an issue where the indices attached to parameter\nnames on a compound model were not handled properly when one or more\nsubmodels have no parameters.  This was especially evident in slicing.", "start_line": 612, "end_line": 636, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_compound_model_with_nonstandard_broadcasting", "qualified_name": "test_compound_model_with_nonstandard_broadcasting", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Ensure that the ``standard_broadcasting`` flag is properly propagated when\ncreating compound models.\n\nSee the commit message for the commit in which this was added for more\ndetails.", "start_line": 639, "end_line": 663, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_compound_model_classify_attributes", "qualified_name": "test_compound_model_classify_attributes", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for an issue raised here:\nhttps://github.com/astropy/astropy/pull/3231#discussion_r22221123\n\nThe issue is that part of the `help` implementation calls a utility\nfunction called `inspect.classify_class_attrs`, which was leading to an\ninfinite recursion.\n\nThis is a useful test in its o", "start_line": 666, "end_line": 684, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_invalid_operands", "qualified_name": "test_invalid_operands", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test that certain operators do not work with models whose inputs/outputs do\nnot match up correctly.", "start_line": 687, "end_line": 703, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_inherit_constraints", "qualified_name": "test_inherit_constraints", "args": ["model"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.parametrize('model', [Gaussian1D(bounds={'stddev': (0, 0.3)}, fixed={'mean': True}) + Gaussian1D(fixed={'mean': True}), (_ConstraintsTestA + _ConstraintsTestB)()])"], "docstring": "Various tests for copying of constraint values between compound models and\ntheir members.\n\nThere are two versions of this test: One where a compound model is created\nfrom two model instances, and another where a compound model is created\nfrom two model classes that have default constraints set on so", "start_line": 727, "end_line": 782, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_compound_custom_inverse", "qualified_name": "test_compound_custom_inverse", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test tha