y taken from the original.\nThe data is assumed to be sliceable and is sliced directly.\n\nWhen possible the return should *", "start_line": 63, "end_line": 94, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_slice_uncertainty", "qualified_name": "_slice_uncertainty", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 96, "end_line": 105, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_slice_mask", "qualified_name": "_slice_mask", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 107, "end_line": 114, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_slice_wcs", "qualified_name": "_slice_wcs", "args": ["self", "item"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 116, "end_line": 123, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "NDSlicingMixin", "bases": [], "methods": ["__getitem__", "_slice", "_slice_uncertainty", "_slice_mask", "_slice_wcs"], "docstring": "Mixin to provide slicing on objects using the `NDData`\ninterface.\n\nThe ``data``, ``mask``, ``uncertainty`` and ``wcs`` will be sliced, if\nset and sliceable. The ``unit`` and ``meta`` will be untouched. The return\nwill be a reference and not a copy, if possible.\n\nExamples\n--------\nUsing this Mixin wi", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 123}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/nddata/mixins/ndio.py", "file_hash": "5f4793263c238f277b5fc0c1d6bbf25f0532011251042bd4b14c25a95403ee68", "imports": [{"module": "io", "names": ["registry"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "read", "qualified_name": "read", "args": ["cls"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Read and parse gridded N-dimensional data and return as an\nNDData-derived object.\n\nThis function provides the NDDataBase interface to the astropy unified\nI/O layer.  This allows easily reading a file in the supported data\nformats.", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 27, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name": "write", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Write a gridded N-dimensional data object out in specified format.\n\nThis function provides the NDDataBase interface to the astropy unified\nI/O layer.  This allows easily writing a file in the supported data\nformats.", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 37, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "NDIOMixin", "bases": [], "methods": ["read", "write"], "docstring": "Mixin class to connect NDData to the astropy input/output registry.\n\nThis mixin adds two methods to its subclasses, ``read`` and ``write``.", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 37}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/nddata/mixins/ndarithmetic.py", "file_hash": "8673fa3df20b8fac1a79c32184e182cfda0dc80c26619f6e14b1c886bb0025b6", "imports": [{"module": "copy", "names": ["deepcopy"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "nduncertainty", "names": ["NDUncertainty"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "units", "names": ["dimensionless_unscaled"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["format_doc", "sharedmethod"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "_arithmetic", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand", "propagate_uncertainties", "handle_mask", "handle_meta", "uncertainty_correlation", "compare_wcs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Base method which calculates the result of the arithmetic operation.\n\nThis method determines the result of the arithmetic operation on the\n``data`` including their units and then forwards to other methods\nto calculate the other properties for the result (like uncertainty).\n\nParameters\n----------\nope", "start_line": 164, "end_line": 285, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arithmetic_data", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic_data", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the resulting data\n\nParameters\n----------\noperation : callable\n    see `NDArithmeticMixin._arithmetic` parameter description.\n\noperand : `NDData`-like instance\n    The second operand wrapped in an instance of the same class as\n    self.\n\nkwds :\n    Additional parameters.\n\nReturns\n-------\nr", "start_line": 287, "end_line": 324, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arithmetic_uncertainty", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic_uncertainty", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand", "result", "correlation"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the resulting uncertainty.\n\nParameters\n----------\noperation : callable\n    see :meth:`NDArithmeticMixin._arithmetic` parameter description.\n\noperand : `NDData`-like instance\n    The second operand wrapped in an instance of the same class as\n    self.\n\nresult : `~astropy.units.Quantity` or ", "start_line": 326, "end_line": 396, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arithmetic_mask", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic_mask", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand", "handle_mask"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the resulting mask\n\nThis is implemented as the piecewise ``or`` operation if both have a\nmask.\n\nParameters\n----------\noperation : callable\n    see :meth:`NDArithmeticMixin._arithmetic` parameter description.\n    By default, the ``operation`` will be ignored.\n\noperand : `NDData`-like instan", "start_line": 398, "end_line": 439, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arithmetic_wcs", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic_wcs", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand", "compare_wcs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the resulting wcs.\n\nThere is actually no calculation involved but it is a good place to\ncompare wcs information of both operands. This is currently not working\nproperly with `~astropy.wcs.WCS` (which is the suggested class for\nstoring as wcs property) but it will not break it neither.\n\nPar", "start_line": 441, "end_line": 486, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_arithmetic_meta", "qualified_name": "_arithmetic_meta", "args": ["self", "operation", "operand", "handle_meta"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculate the resulting meta.\n\nParameters\n----------\noperation : callable\n    see :meth:`NDArithmeticMixin._arithmetic` parameter description.\n    By default, the ``operation`` will be ignored.\n\noperand : `NDData`-like instance\n    The second operand wrapped in an instance of the same class as\n    s", "start_line": 488, "end_line": 514, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add", "qualified_name": "add", "args": ["self", "operand", "operand2"], "decorators": ["sharedmethod", "format_doc(_arit_doc, name='addition', op='+')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 518, "end_line": 520, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "subtract", "qualified_name": "subtract", "args": ["self", "operand", "operand2"], "decorators": ["sharedmethod", "format_doc(_arit_doc, name='subtraction', op='-')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 524, "end_line": 526, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "multiply", "qualified_name": "multiply", "args": ["self", "operand", "operand2"], "decorators": ["sharedmethod", "format_doc(_arit_doc, name='multiplication', op='*')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 530, "end_line": 532, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "divide", "qualified_name": "divide", "args": ["self", "operand", "operand2"], "decorators": ["sharedmethod", "format_doc(_arit_doc, name='division', op='/')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 536, "end_line": 538, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_prepare_then_do_arithmetic", "qualified_name": "_prepare_then_do_arithmetic", "args": ["self_or_cls", "operation", "operand", "operand2"], "decorators": ["sharedmethod"], "docstring": "Intermediate method called by public arithmetics (i.e. ``add``)\nbefore the processing method (``_