('not HAS_SCIPY')"], "docstring": "Test intervals against those published in Gehrels 1986\n\nNote: I think there's a typo (transposition of digits) in Gehrels 1986,\nspecifically for the two-sigma lower limit for 3 events; they claim\n0.569 but this function returns 0.59623...", "start_line": 506, "end_line": 528, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_poisson_conf_frequentist_confidence_gehrels_3sigma", "qualified_name": "test_poisson_conf_frequentist_confidence_gehrels_3sigma", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.skipif('not HAS_SCIPY')"], "docstring": "Test intervals against those published in Gehrels 1986", "start_line": 532, "end_line": 549, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_poisson_conf_gehrels86", "qualified_name": "test_poisson_conf_gehrels86", "args": ["n"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.skipif('not HAS_SCIPY')", "pytest.mark.parametrize('n', [0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 20, 100])"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 554, "end_line": 558, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_scipy_poisson_limit", "qualified_name": "test_scipy_poisson_limit", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.skipif('not HAS_SCIPY')"], "docstring": "Test that the lower-level routine gives the snae number.\n\nTest numbers are from table1 1, 3 in\nKraft, Burrows and Nousek in\n`ApJ 374, 344 (1991) <http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1991ApJ...374..344K>`_", "start_line": 562, "end_line": 575, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_mpmath_poisson_limit", "qualified_name": "test_mpmath_poisson_limit", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.skipif('not HAS_MPMATH')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 579, "end_line": 583, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_poisson_conf_value_errors", "qualified_name": "test_poisson_conf_value_errors", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.skipif('not HAS_SCIPY')"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 587, "end_line": 603, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_poisson_conf_