as a new\nmodule in this package.  Any \"self\" transformations (i.e., those that transform\nfrom one frame to another frame of the same class) should be included in that\nmodule.  Transformation functions connecting the new frame to other frames\nshould be in a separate module, which should be imported in this package's\n``__init__.py`` to ensure the transformations are hooked up when this package is\nimported.  Placing the trasnformation functions in separate modules avoids\ncircular dependencies, because they need references to the frame classes.", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/coordinates/builtin_frames/skyoffset.py", "file_hash": "7645d3ddc635d04dce3c73ae706464c8d7443af300636500ebac754902ab8245", "imports": [{"module": "", "names": ["units"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.compat", "names": ["namedtuple_asdict"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["representation"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "transformations", "names": ["DynamicMatrixTransform", "FunctionTransform"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "baseframe", "names": ["frame_transform_graph", "RepresentationMapping", "BaseCoordinateFrame"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "attributes", "names": ["CoordinateAttribute", "QuantityAttribute"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "matrix_utilities", "names": ["rotation_matrix", "matrix_product", "matrix_transpose"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "make_skyoffset_cls", "qualified_name": "make_skyoffset_cls", "args": ["framecls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new class that is the sky offset frame for a specific class of\norigin frame. If such a class has already been created for this frame, the\nsame class will be returned.\n\nThe new class will always have component names for spherical coordinates of\n``lon``/``lat``.\n\nParameters\n----------\nframecl", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 150, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name"