ration.", "start_line": 177, "end_line": 185, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_astroyear", "qualified_name": "check_astroyear", "args": ["year", "field", "config", "pos"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Raises a `~astropy.io.votable.exceptions.VOTableSpecError` if\n*year* is not a valid astronomical year as defined by the VOTABLE\nstandard.\n\nParameters\n----------\nyear : str\n    An astronomical year string\n\nfield : str\n    The name of the field this year was found in (used for error\n    message)\n\nconf", "start_line": 190, "end_line": 212, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_string", "qualified_name": "check_string", "args": ["string", "attr_name", "config", "pos"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Raises a `~astropy.io.votable.exceptions.VOTableSpecError` if\n*string* is not a string or Unicode string.\n\nParameters\n----------\nstring : str\n    An astronomical year string\n\nattr_name : str\n    The name of the field this year was found in (used for error\n    message)\n\nconfig, pos : optional\n    Inf", "start_line": 215, "end_line": 235, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "resolve_id", "qualified_name": "resolve_id", "args": ["ID", "id", "config", "pos"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 238, "end_line": 242, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "check_ucd", "qualified_name": "check_ucd", "args": ["ucd", "config", "pos"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Warns or raises a\n`~astropy.io.votable.exceptions.VOTableSpecError` if *ucd* is not\na valid `unified content descriptor`_ string as defined by the\nVOTABLE standard.\n\nParameters\n----------\nucd : str\n    A UCD string.\n\nconfig, pos : optional\n    Information about the source of the value", "start_line": 245, "end_line": 276, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookup_by_attr", "qualified_name": "lookup_by_attr", "args": ["self", "ref", "before"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a string *ref*, finds the first element in the iterator\nwhere the given attribute == *ref*.  If *before* is provided,\nwill stop searching at the object *before*.  This is\nimportant, since \"forward references\" are not allowed in the\nVOTABLE format.", "start_line": 104, "end_line": 120, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookup_by_attr_unique", "qualified_name": "lookup_by_attr_unique", "args": ["self", "ref", "before"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 122, "end_line": 127, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookup_by_id_or_name", "qualified_name": "lookup_by_id_or_name", "args": ["self", "ref", "before"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given an key *ref*, finds the first element in the iterator\nwith the attribute ID == *ref* or name == *ref*.  If *before*\nis provided, will stop searching at the object *before*.  This\nis important, since \"forward references\" are not allowed in\nthe VOTABLE format.", "start_line": 143, "end_line": 162, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ID", "qualified_name": "ID", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "The XML ID_ of the element.  May be `None` or a string\nconforming to XML ID_ syntax.", "start_line": 283, "end_line": 288, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ID", "qualified_name": "ID", "args": ["self", "ID"], "decorators": ["ID.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 291, "end_line": 293, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "ID", "qualified_name": "ID", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["ID.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 296, "end_line": 297, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "An optional name for the element.", "start_line": 302, "end_line": 304, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "name", "qualified_name": "name", "args": ["self", "name"], "decorators": ["name.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_