"is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "datatype", "qualified_name": "datatype", "args": ["self", "datatype"], "decorators": ["datatype.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1295, "end_line": 1303, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "precision", "qualified_name": "precision", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Along with :attr:`width`, defines the `numerical accuracy`_\nassociated with the data.  These values are used to limit the\nprecision when writing floating point values back to the XML\nfile.  Otherwise, it is purely informational -- the Numpy\nrecarray containing the data itself does not use this\ninfor", "start_line": 1306, "end_line": 1315, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "precision", "qualified_name": "precision", "args": ["self", "precision"], "decorators": ["precision.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1318, "end_line": 1321, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "precision", "qualified_name": "precision", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["precision.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1324, "end_line": 1325, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "width", "qualified_name": "width", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Along with :attr:`precision`, defines the `numerical\naccuracy`_ associated with the data.  These values are used to\nlimit the precision when writing floating point values back to\nthe XML file.  Otherwise, it is purely informational -- the\nNumpy recarray containing the data itself does not use this\ni", "start_line": 1328, "end_line": 1337, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "width", "qualified_name": "width", "args": ["self", "width"], "decorators": ["width.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1340, "end_line": 1345, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "width", "qualified_name": "width", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["width.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1348, "end_line