 will *not* be called if the row already matches the header.\n\nParameters\n----------\nstr_vals : list\n    A list of value strings from the current row of the table.\nnco", "start_line": 280, "end_line": 303, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_type_map_key", "qualified_name": "get_type_map_key", "args": ["self", "col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 313, "end_line": 314, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_cols", "qualified_name": "get_cols", "args": ["self", "lines"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Initialize the header Column objects from the table ``lines``.\n\nThis is a specialized get_cols for the RDB type:\nLine 0: RDB col names\nLine 1: RDB col definitions\nLine 2+: RDB data rows\n\n\nParameters\n----------\nlines : list\n    List of table lines\n\nReturns\n-------\nNone", "start_line": 316, "end_line": 351, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name": "write", "args": ["self", "lines"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 353, "end_line": 361, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "BasicHeader", "bases": ["core.BaseHeader"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Basic table Header Reader\n\nSet a few defaults for common ascii table formats\n(start at line 0, comments begin with ``#`` and possibly white space)", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 27}, {"name": "BasicData", "bases": ["core.BaseData"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Basic table Data Reader\n\nSet a few defaults for common ascii table formats\n(start at line 1, comments begin with ``#`` and possibly white space)", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 39}, {"name": "Basic", "bases": ["core.BaseReader"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Read a character-delimited table with a single header line at the top\nfollowed by data lines to the end of the table.  Lines beginning with # as\nthe first non-whitespace character are comments.  This reader is highly\nconfigurable.\n::\n\n    rdr = ascii.get_reader(Reader=ascii.Basic)\n    rdr.header.spl", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 73}, {"name": "NoHeaderHeader", "bases": ["BasicHeader"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Reader for table header without a header\n\nSet the start of header line number to `None`, which tells the basic\nreader there is no header line.", "start_line": 76, "end_line": 83}, {"name": "NoHeaderData", "bases": ["BasicData"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Reader for table data without a header\n\nData starts at first uncommented line since there is no header line.", "start_line": 86, "end_line": 92}, {"name": "NoHeader", "bases": ["Basic"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Read a table with no header line.  Columns are autonamed using\nheader.auto_format which defaults to \"col%d\".  Otherwise this reader\nthe same as the :class:`Basic` class from which it is derived.  Example::\n\n  # Table data\n  1 2 \"hello there\"\n  3 4 world", "start_line": 95, "end_line": 108}, {"name": "CommentedHeaderHeader", "bases": ["BasicHeader"], "methods": ["process_lines", "write"], "docstring": "Header class for which the column definition line starts with the\ncomment character.  See the :class:`CommentedHeader` class  for an example.", "start_line": 111, "end_line": 129}, {"name": "CommentedHeader", "bases": ["Basic"], "methods": ["read", "write_header"], "docstring": "Read a file where the column names are given in a line that begins with\nthe header comment character. ``header_start`` can be used to specify the\nline index of column names, and it can be a negative index (for example -1\nfor the last commented line).  The default delimiter is the <space>\ncharacter.:", "start_line": 132, "end_line": 172}, {"name": "TabHeaderSplitter", "bases": ["core.DefaultSplitter"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Split lines on tab and do not remove whitespace", "start_line": 175, "end_line": 178}, {"name": "TabDataSplitter", "bases": ["TabHeaderSplitter"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Don't strip data value whitespace since that is significant in TSV tables", "start_line": 181, "end_line": 186}, {"name": "TabHeader", "bases": ["BasicHeader"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Reader for header of tables with tab separated header", "start_line": 189, "end_line": 193}, {"name": "TabData", "bases": ["BasicData"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Reader for data of tables with tab separated data", "start_line": 196, "end_line": 200}, {"name": "Tab", "bases": ["Basic"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Read a tab-separated file.  Unlike the :class:`Basic` reader, whitespace is\nnot stripped from the beginning and end of either lines or individual column\nvalues.\n\nExample::\n\n  col1 <tab> col2 <tab> col3\n  # Comment line\n  1 <tab> 2 <tab> 5", "start_line": 203, "end_line": 218}, {"name": "CsvSplitter", "bases": ["core.DefaultSplitter"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Split on comma for CSV (comma-separated-value) tables", "start_line": 221, "end_line": 225}, {"name": "CsvHeader", "bases": ["BasicHeader"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Header that uses the :class:`astropy.io.ascii.basic.CsvSplitter`", "start_line": 228, "end_line": 234}, {"name": "CsvData", "bases": ["BasicData"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Data that uses the :class:`astropy.io.ascii.basic.CsvSplitter`", "start_line": 237, "end_line": 244}, {"name": "Csv", "bases": ["Basic"], "methods": ["inconsistent_handler"], "docstring": "Read a CSV (comma-separated-values) file.\n\nExample::\n\n  num,ra,dec,radius,mag\n  1,32.23222,10.1211,0.8,18.1\n  2,38.12321,-88.1321,2.2,17.0\n\nPlain csv (comma separated value) files typically contain as many entries\nas there are columns on each line. In contrast, common spreadsheet editors\nstop writin", "start_line": 247, "end_line": 303}, {"name": "RdbHeader", "bases": ["TabHeader"], "methods": ["get_type_map_key", "get_cols", "write"], "docstring": "Header for RDB tables", "start_line": 306, "end_line": 361}, {"name": "RdbData", "bases": ["TabData"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Data reader for RDB data. Starts reading at line 2.", "start_line": 364, "end_line": 368}, {"name": "Rdb", "bases": ["Tab"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Read a tab-separated file with an extra line after the column definition\nline.  The RDB format meets this definition.  Example::\n\n  col1 <tab> col2 <tab> col3\n  N <tab> S <tab> N\n  1 <tab> 2 <tab> 5\n\nIn this reader the second line is just ignored.", "start_line": 371, "end_line": 388}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "An extensible ASCII table reader and writer.\n\nbasic.py:\n  Basic table read / write functionality for simple character\n  delimited files with various options for column header definition.\n\n:Copyright: Smithsonian Astrophysical Observatory (2011)\n:Author: Tom Aldcroft (aldcroft@head.cfa.harvard.edu)", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/ascii/sextractor.py", "file_hash": "984c3e79d031960de0ee2166a7cc87b1486bbac661f9a28223dd15e8002fe421", "imports": [{"module": "re", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "", "names": ["core"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "get_cols", "qualified_name": "get_cols", "args": ["self", "lines"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Initialize the header Column objects from the table ``lines`` for a SExtractor\nheader.  The SExtractor header is specialized so that we just copy the entire BaseHeader\nget_cols routine and modify as needed.\n\nParameters\n----------\nlines : list\n    List of table lines", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 96, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "read", "qualified_name": "read", "args": ["self", "table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Read input data (file-like object, filename, list of strings, or\nsingle string) into a Table and return the result.", "start_line": 137, "end_line": 146, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "write", "qualified_name": "write", "args": ["self", "table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 148, "end_line": 149, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], 