 "args": ["self", "order"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The Numpy documentation lies; `numpy.ndarray.copy` is not equivalent to\n`numpy.copy`.  Differences include that it re-views the copied array as\nself's ndarray subclass, as though it were taking a slice; this means\n``__array_finalize__`` is called and the copy shares all the array\nattributes (includi", "start_line": 552, "end_line": 566, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "columns", "qualified_name": "columns", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A user-visible accessor for the coldefs.\n\nSee https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/44", "start_line": 569, "end_line": 576, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_coldefs", "qualified_name": "_coldefs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 579, "end_line": 596, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_coldefs", "qualified_name": "_coldefs", "args": ["self", "cols"], "decorators": ["_coldefs.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 599, "end_line": 603, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_coldefs", "qualified_name": "_coldefs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["_coldefs.deleter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 606, "end_line": 610, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__del__", "qualified_name": "__del__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 612, "end_line": 623, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "names", "qualified_name": "names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "List of column names.", "start_line": 626, "end_line": 634, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "formats", "qualified_name": "formats", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "List of column FITS formats.", "start_line": 637, "end_line": 643, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_raw_itemsize", "qualified_name": "_raw_itemsize", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns the size of row items that would be written to the raw FITS\nfile, taking into account the possibility of unicode columns being\ncompactified.\n\nCurrently for internal use only.", "start_line": 646, "end_line": 665, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "field", "qualified_name": "field", "args": ["self", "key"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A view of a `Column`'s data as an array.", "start_line": 667, "end_line": 715, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_cache_field", "qualified_name": "_cache_field", "args": ["self", "name", "field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Do not store fields in _converted if one of its bases is self,\nor if it has a common base with self.\n\nThis results in a reference cycle that cannot be broken since\nndarrays do not participate in cyclic garbage collection.", "start_line": 717, "end_line": 743, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_column_attribute_changed", "qualified_name": "_update_column_attribute_changed", "args": ["self", "column", "idx", "attr", "old_value", "new_value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update how the data is formatted depending on changes to column\nattributes initiated by the user through the `Column` interface.\n\nDispatches column attribute change notifications to individual methods\nfor each attribute ``_update_column_<attr>``", "start_line": 745, "end_line": 759, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_column_name", "qualified_name": "_update_column_name", "args": ["self", "column", "idx", "old_name", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the dtype field names when a column name is changed.", "start_line": 761, "end_line": 766, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_x", "qualified_name": "_convert_x", "args": ["self", "field", "recformat"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a raw table column to a bit array as specified by the\nFITS X format.", "start_line": 768, "end_line": 775, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_p", "qualified_name": "_convert_p", "args": ["self", "column", "field", "recformat"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a raw table column of FITS P or Q format descriptors\nto a VLA column with the array data returned from the heap.", "start_line": 777, "end_line": 817, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_ascii", "qualified_name": "_convert_ascii", "args": ["self", "column", "field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Special handling for ASCII table columns to convert columns containing\nnumeric types to actual numeric arrays from the string representation.", "start_line": 819, "end_line": 858, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_other", "qualified_name": "_convert_other", "args": ["self", "column", "field", "recformat"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform conversions on any other fixed-width column data types.\n\nThis may not perform any conversion at all if it's not necessary, in\nwhich case the original column array is returned.", "start_line": 860, "end_line": 985, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_heap_data", "qualified_name": "_get_heap_data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a pointer into the table's raw data to its heap (if present).\n\nThis is returned as a numpy byte array.", "start_line": 987, "end_line": 999, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_raw_data", "qualified_name": "_get_raw_data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns the base array of self that \"raw data array\" that is the\narray in the format that it was first read from a file before it was\nsliced or viewed as a different type in any way.\n\nThis is determined by walking through the bases until finding one that\nhas at least the same number of bytes as self", "start_line": 1001, "end_line": 1023, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_scale_factors", "