allow us to deal with scaled columns.  It also handles\nconversion/scaling of columns in ASCII tables.  The `FITS_record`\nclass expects a `FITS_rec` object as input.", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 141}, {"name": "FITS_rec", "bases": ["np.recarray"], "methods": ["__new__", "__setstate__", "__reduce__", "__array_finalize__", "_init", "from_columns", "__repr__", "__getitem__", "__setitem__", "copy", "columns", "_coldefs", "_coldefs", "_coldefs", "__del__", "names", "formats", "_raw_itemsize", "field", "_cache_field", "_update_column_attribute_changed", "_update_column_name", "_convert_x", "_convert_p", "_convert_ascii", "_convert_other", "_get_heap_data", "_get_raw_data", "_get_scale_factors", "_scale_back", "_scale_back_strings", "_scale_back_ascii"], "docstring": "FITS record array class.\n\n`FITS_rec` is the data part of a table HDU's data part.  This is a layer\nover the `~numpy.recarray`, so we can deal with scaled columns.\n\nIt inherits all of the standard methods from `numpy.ndarray`.", "start_line": 144, "end_line": 1264}, {"name": "_UnicodeArrayEncodeError", "bases": ["UnicodeEncodeError"], "methods": ["__init__"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1284, "end_line": 1287}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/fits/file.py", "file_hash": "6f84a14db2d22c50175e490e84d3a966c934cc7b90d8cbfc7835611e9cd239df", "imports": [{"module": "bz2", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "gzip", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "http.client", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "mmap", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "operator", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "pathlib", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "io", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "os", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "sys", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "tempfile", "na