: "Given the column-specific time reference frame information, verify that\neach column-specific time coordinate attribute has a valid value.\nReturn True if the coordinate column is time, or else return False.\n\nParameters\n----------\nglobal_info : dict\n    Global time reference frame information.\ncolumn_", "start_line": 168, "end_line": 275, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_info_if_time_column", "qualified_name": "_get_info_if_time_column", "args": ["col", "global_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check if a column without corresponding time column keywords in the\nFITS header represents time or not. If yes, return the time column\ninformation needed for its conversion to Time.\nThis is only applicable to the special-case where a column has the\nname 'TIME' and a time unit.", "start_line": 278, "end_line": 305, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_global_time", "qualified_name": "_convert_global_time", "args": ["table", "global_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert the table metadata for time informational keywords\nto astropy Time.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntable : `~astropy.table.Table`\n    The table whose time metadata is to be converted.\nglobal_info : dict\n    Global time reference frame information.", "start_line": 308, "end_line": 343, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_convert_time_column", "qualified_name": "_convert_time_column", "args": ["col", "column_info"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert time columns to astropy Time columns.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncol : `~astropy.table.Column`\n    The time coordinate column to be converted to Time.\ncolumn_info : dict\n    Column-specific time reference frame override information.", "start_line": 346, "end_line": 404, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fits_to_time", "qualified_name": "fits_to_time", "args": ["hdr", "table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Read FITS binary table time columns as `~astropy.time.Time`.\n\nThis method reads the metadata associated with time coordinates, as\nstored in a FITS binary table header, converts time columns into\n`~astropy.time.Time` columns and reads global reference times as\n`~astropy.time.Time` instances.\n\nParamet", "start_line": 407, "end_line": 474, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "time_to_fits", "qualified_name": "time_to_fits", "args": ["table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Replace Time columns in a Table with non-mixin columns containing\neach element as a vector of two doubles (jd1, jd2) and return a FITS\nheader with appropriate time coordinate keywords.\njd = jd1 + jd2 represents time in the Julian Date format with\nhigh-precision.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntable : `~astr", "start_line": 477, "end_line": 568, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/fits/verify.py", "file_hash": "1618a7f018fa0bc666e1251dbe7be4782471eb9c2bfbaf66101d6c3d0c24c177", "imports": [{"module": "operator", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils", "names": ["indent"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "utils.exceptions", "names": ["AstropyUserWarning"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}], "functions": [{"name": "run_option", "qualified_name": "run_option", "args": ["self", "option", "err_text", "fix_text", "fix", "fixable"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Execute the verification with selected option.", "start_line": 32, "end_line": 50, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "verify", "qualified_name": "verify", "args": ["self", "option"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Verify all values in the instance.\n\nParameters\n----------\noption : str\n    Output verification option.  Must be one of ``\"fix\"``,\n    ``\"silentfix\"``, ``\"ignore\"``, ``\"warn\"``, or\n    ``\"exception\"``.  May also be any combination of ``\