nteger, it is the index\nin the list.  If string,\n\n    a. Field (column) names are case sensitive: you can have two\n       different columns called 'abc' and 'ABC' respectively.\n\n    b. When you *refer*", "start_line": 1930, "end_line": 1973, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_unwrapx", "qualified_name": "_unwrapx", "args": ["input", "output", "repeat"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Unwrap the X format column into a Boolean array.\n\nParameters\n----------\ninput\n    input ``Uint8`` array of shape (`s`, `nbytes`)\n\noutput\n    output Boolean array of shape (`s`, `repeat`)\n\nrepeat\n    number of bits", "start_line": 1976, "end_line": 1998, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_wrapx", "qualified_name": "_wrapx", "args": ["input", "output", "repeat"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Wrap the X format column Boolean array into an ``UInt8`` array.\n\nParameters\n----------\ninput\n    input Boolean array of shape (`s`, `repeat`)\n\noutput\n    output ``Uint8`` array of shape (`s`, `nbytes`)\n\nrepeat\n    number of bits", "start_line": 2001, "end_line": 2029, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_makep", "qualified_name": "_makep", "args": ["array", "descr_output", "format", "nrows"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Construct the P (or Q) format column array, both the data descriptors and\nthe data.  It returns the output \"data\" array of data type `dtype`.\n\nThe descriptor location will have a zero offset for all columns\nafter this call.  The final offset will be calculated when the file\nis written.\n\nParameters\n-", "start_line": 2032, "end_line": 2091, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse_tformat", "qualified_name": "_parse_tformat", "args": ["tform"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parse ``TFORMn`` keyword for a binary table into a\n``(repeat, format, option)`` tuple.", "start_line": 2094, "end_line": 2112, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_parse_ascii_tformat", "qualifi