is\n    ``\"all\"`` which will print out all attributes.  It forgives plurals\n    and blanks.  If", "start_line": 1745, "end_line": 1794, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "input", "ascii"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1803, "end_line": 1814, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "dtype", "qualified_name": "dtype", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1817, "end_line": 1824, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "spans", "qualified_name": "spans", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "A list of the widths of each field in the table.", "start_line": 1827, "end_line": 1830, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_recformats", "qualified_name": "_recformats", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1833, "end_line": 1843, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_col", "qualified_name": "add_col", "args": ["self", "column"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1845, "end_line": 1847, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "del_col", "qualified_name": "del_col", "args": ["self", "col_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1849, "end_line": 1851, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_field_metrics", "qualified_name": "_update_field_metrics", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Updates the list of the start columns, the list of the widths of each\nfield, and the total width of each record in the table.", "start_line": 1853, "end_line": 1873, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__new__", "qualified_name": "__new__", "args": ["cls", "input", "dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Parameters\n----------\ninput\n    a sequence of variable-sized elements.", "start_line": 1882, "end_line": 1904, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__array_finalize__", "qualified_name": "__array_finalize__", "args": ["self", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1906, "end_line": 1910, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__setitem__", "qualified_name": "__setitem__", "args": ["self", "key", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "To make sure the new item has consistent data type to avoid\nmisalignment.", "start_line": 1912, "end_line": 1927, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "convert_int", "qualified_name": "convert_int", "args": ["val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2152, "end_line": 2160, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Delayed", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__getitem__"], "docstring": "Delayed file-reading data.", "start_line": 136, "end_line": 148}, {"name": "_BaseColumnFormat", "bases": ["str"], "methods": ["__eq__", "__hash__", "dtype", "from_column_format"], "docstring": "Base class for binary table column formats (just called _ColumnFormat)\nand ASCII table column formats (_AsciiColumnFormat).", "start_line": 151, "end_line": 192}, {"name": "_ColumnFormat", "bases": ["_BaseColumnFormat"], "methods": ["__new__", "from_recformat", "recformat", "canonical"], "docstring": "Represents a FITS binary table column format.\n\nThis is an enhancement over using a normal string for the format, since the\nrepeat count, format code, and option are available as separate attributes,\nand smart comparison is used.  For example 1J == J.", "start_line": 195, "end_line": 248}, {"name": "_AsciiColumnFormat", "bases": ["_BaseColumnFormat"], "methods": ["__new__", "from_column_format", "from_recformat", "recformat", "canonical"], "docstring": "Similar to _ColumnFormat but specifically for columns in ASCII tables.\n\nThe formats of ASCII table columns and binary table columns are inherently\nincompatible in FITS.  They don't support the same ranges and types of\nvalues, and even reuse format codes in subtly different ways.  For example\nthe for", "start_line": 251, "end_line": 312}, {"name": "_FormatX", "bases": ["str"], "methods": ["__new__", "__getnewargs__", "tform"], "docstring": "For X format in binary tables.", "start_line": 315, "end_line": 330}, {"name": "_FormatP", "bases": ["str"], "methods": ["__new__", "__getnewargs__", "from_tform", "tform"], "docstring": "For P format in variable length table.", "start_line": 336, "end_line": 374}, {"name": "_FormatQ", "bases": ["_FormatP"], "methods": [], "docstring": "Carries type description of the Q format for variable length arrays.\n\nThe Q format is like the P format but uses 64-bit integers in the array\ndescriptors, allowing for heaps stored beyond 2GB into a file.", "start_line": 377, "end_line": 386}, {"name": "ColumnAttribute", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "__get__", "__set__", "__call__", "__repr__"], "docstring": "Descriptor for attributes of `Column` that are associated with keywords\nin the FITS header and describe properties of the column as specified in\nthe FITS standard.\n\nEach `ColumnAttribute` may have a ``validator`` method defined on it.\nThis validates values set on this attribute to ensure that they m", "start_line": 389, "end_line": 458}, {"name": "Column", "bases": ["NotifierMixin"], "methods": ["__init__", "__repr__", "__eq__", "__hash__", "array", "array", "array", "name", "coord_type", "coord_unit", "coord_ref_point", "coord_ref_value", "coord_inc", "time_ref_pos", "ascii", "dtype", "copy", "_convert_format", "_verify_keywords", "_determine_formats", "_guess_format", "_convert_to_valid_data_type"], "docstring": "Class which contains the definition of one column, e.g.  ``ttype``,\n``tform``, etc. and the array containing values for the column.", "start_line": 461, "end_line": 1267}, {"name": "ColDefs", "bases": ["NotifierMixin"], "methods": ["__new__", "__getnewargs__", "__init__", "_init_from_coldefs", "_init_from_sequence", "_init_from_array", "_init_from_table", "__copy__", "__deepcopy__", "_copy_column", "__getattr__", "dtype", "names", "formats", "_arrays", "_recformats", "_dims", "__getitem__", "__len__", "__repr__", "__add__", "__radd__", "__sub__", "_update_column_attribute_changed", "add_col", "del_col", "change_attrib", "change_name", "change_unit", "info"], "docstring": "Column definitions class.\n\nIt has attributes corresponding to the `Column` attributes\n(e.g. `ColDefs` has the attribute ``names`` while `Column`\nhas ``name``). Each attribute in `ColDefs` is a list of\ncorresponding attribute values from all `Column` objects.", "start_line": 1270, "end_line": 1794}, {"name": "_AsciiColDefs", "bases": ["ColDefs"], "methods": ["__init__", "dtype", "spans", "_recformats", "add_col", "del_col", "_update_field_metrics"], "docstring": "ColDefs implementation for ASCII tables.", "start_line": 1797, "end_line": 1873}, {"name": "_VLF", "bases": ["np.ndarray"], "methods": ["__new__", "__array_finalize__", "__setitem__"], "docstring": "Variable length field object.", "start_line": 1879, "end_line": 1927}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "astropy/io/fits/convenience.py", "file_hash": "f5ba2049809e4ebe76c0ad048bba0145528f72c7fa5d5a5e0a549ff88400074b", "imports": [{"module": "operator", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "os", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "warnings", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": ""}, {"module": "numpy", "names": [], "is_from": false, "alias": "np"}, {"module": "diff", "names": ["FITSDiff", "HDUDiff"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "file", "names": ["FILE_MODES", "_File"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.base", "names": ["_BaseHDU", "_ValidHDU"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.hdulist", "names": ["fitsopen", "HDUList"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.image", "names": ["PrimaryHDU", "ImageHDU"], "is_from": true, "alias": ""}, {"module": "hdu.table", "names": ["BinTableHDU"], "is_fr