es argument list can overlap with the existing column names.\nThis tests the issue in #1991.", "start_line": 853, "end_line": 859, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_sextractor_units", "qualified_name": "test_sextractor_units", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make sure that the SExtractor reader correctly inputs descriptions and units.", "start_line": 862, "end_line": 881, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_sextractor_last_column_array", "qualified_name": "test_sextractor_last_column_array", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make sure that the SExtractor reader handles the last column correctly when it is array-like.", "start_line": 884, "end_line": 907, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_list_with_newlines", "qualified_name": "test_list_with_newlines", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "    Check that lists of strings where some strings consist of just a newline\n    (\"\n\") are parsed correctly.\n    ", "start_line": 910, "end_line": 919, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_commented_csv", "qualified_name": "test_commented_csv", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check that Csv reader does not have ignore lines with the # comment\ncharacter which is defined for most Basic readers.", "start_line": 922, "end_line": 930, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_meta_comments", "qualified_name": "test_meta_comments", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make sure that line comments are included in the ``meta`` attribute\nof the output Table.", "start_line": 933, "end_line": 940, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_guess_fail", "qualified_name": "test_guess_fail", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check the error message when guess fails", "start_line": 943, "end_line": 959, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_guessing_file_object", "qualified_name": "test_guessing_file_object", "args": [], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.xfail('not HAS_BZ2')"], "docstring": "Test guessing a file object.  Fixes #3013 and similar issue noted in #3019.", "start_line": 963, "end_line": 968, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_pformat_roundtrip", "qualified_name": "test_pformat_roundtrip", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check that the screen output of ``print tab`` can be read. See #3025.", "start_line": 971, "end_line": 982, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_ipac_abbrev", "qualified_name": "test_ipac_abbrev", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 985, "end_line": 995, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_almost_but_not_quite_daophot", "qualified_name": "test_almost_but_not_quite_daophot", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for #3319.\nThis tables looks so close to a daophot table, that the daophot reader gets\nquite far before it fails with an AttributeError.\n\nNote that this table will actually be read as Commented Header table with\nthe columns ['some', 'header', 'info'].", "start_line": 998, "end_line": 1012, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_commented_header_comments", "qualified_name": "test_commented_header_comments", "args": ["fast"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.parametrize('fast', [True, False])"], "docstring": "Test that comments in commented_header are as expected and that the\ntable round-trips.", "start_line": 1016, "end_line": 1037, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_probably_html", "qualified_name": "test_probably_html", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Test the routine for guessing if a table input to ascii.read is probably HTML", "start_line": 1040, "end_line": 1067, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_data_header_start", "qualified_name": "test_data_header_start", "args": ["fast_reader"], "decorators": ["pytest.mark.parametrize('fast_reader', [True, False, 'force'