----\nfileobj : file object or file-like object\n    Input FITS file.  The file's seek p", "start_line": 298, "end_line": 333, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "writeto", "qualified_name": "writeto", "args": ["self", "name", "output_verify", "overwrite", "checksum"], "decorators": ["deprecated_renamed_argument('clobber', 'overwrite', '2.0')"], "docstring": "Write the HDU to a new file. This is a convenience method to\nprovide a user easier output interface if only one HDU needs\nto be written to a file.\n\nParameters\n----------\nname : file path, file object or file-like object\n    Output FITS file.  If the file object is already opened, it must\n    be open", "start_line": 336, "end_line": 373, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_readfrom_internal", "qualified_name": "_readfrom_internal", "args": ["cls", "data", "header", "checksum", "ignore_missing_end"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Provides the bulk of the internal implementation for readfrom and\nfromstring.\n\nFor some special cases, supports using a header that was already\ncreated, and just using the input data for the actual array data.", "start_line": 376, "end_line": 460, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_raw_data", "qualified_name": "_get_raw_data", "args": ["self", "shape", "code", "offset"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return raw array from either the HDU's memory buffer or underlying\nfile.", "start_line": 462, "end_line": 477, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_prewriteto", "qualified_name": "_prewriteto", "args": ["self", "checksum", "inplace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 483, "end_line": 487, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_uint_scale_keywords", "qualified_name": "_update_uint_scale_keywords", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If the data is unsigned int 16, 32, or 64 add BSCALE/BZERO cards to\nheader.", "start_line": 489, "end_line": 506, "is_asy