te to\nthe new file.\n\nIf this pr", "start_line": 614, "end_line": 629, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_writeto", "qualified_name": "_writeto", "args": ["self", "fileobj", "inplace", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 635, "end_line": 642, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_writeto_internal", "qualified_name": "_writeto_internal", "args": ["self", "fileobj", "inplace", "copy"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 644, "end_line": 707, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_close", "qualified_name": "_close", "args": ["self", "closed"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 709, "end_line": 716, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "size", "qualified_name": "size", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns the size (in bytes) of the HDU's data part.", "start_line": 748, "end_line": 758, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_summary", "qualified_name": "_summary", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 760, "end_line": 761, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "verify", "qualified_name": "verify", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 763, "end_line": 764, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "match_header", "qualified_name": "match_header", "args": ["cls", "header"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Matches any HDU that has the 'SIMPLE' keyword but is not a standard\nPrimary or Groups HDU.", "start_line": 785, "end_line": 802, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "size", "qualified_name": "size", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Returns the size (in bytes) of the HDU's data part.", "start_line": 805, "end_line": 813, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_writedata", "qualified_name": "_writedata", "args": ["self", "fileobj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Differs from the base class :class:`_writedata` in that it doesn't\nautomatically add padding, and treats the data as a string of raw bytes\ninstead of an array.", "start_line": 815, "end_line": 840, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_summary", "qualified_name": "_summary", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 842, "end_line": 843, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "data", "qualified_name": "data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "Return the file data.", "start_line": 846, "end_line": 851, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_verify", "qualified_name": "_verify", "args": ["self", "option"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 853, "end_line": 860, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "data", "header", "name", "ver"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 868, "end_line": 881, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "match_header", "qualified_name": "match_header", "args": ["cls", "header"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Matches any HDU that is not recognized as having either the SIMPLE or\nXTENSION keyword in its header's first card, but is nonetheless not\ncorrupted.\n\nTODO: Maybe it would make more sense to use _NonstandardHDU in this\ncase?  Not sure...", "start_line": 884, "end_line": 894, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "size", "qualified_name": "size", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Size (in bytes) of the data portion of the HDU.", "start_line": 897, "end_line": 912, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "filebytes", "qualified_name": "filebytes", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Calculates and returns the number of bytes that this HDU will write to\na file.", "start_line": 914, "end_line": 922, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "fileinfo", "qualified_name": "fileinfo", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Returns a dictionary detailing information about the locations\nof this HDU within any associated file.  The values are only\nvalid after a read or write of the associated file with no\nintervening changes to the `HDUList`.\n\nReturns\n-------\ndict or None\n\n   The dictionary details information about the ", "start_line": 924, "end_line": 958, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "copy", "qualified_name": "copy", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Make a copy of the HDU, both header and data are copied.", "start_line": 960, "end_line": 969, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_verify", "qualified_name": "_verify", "args": ["self", "option"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 971, "end_line": 1036, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "req_cards", "qualified_name": "req_cards", "args": ["self", "keyword", "pos", "test", "fix_value", "option", "errlist"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check the existence, location, and value of a required `Card`.\n\nParameters\n----------\nkeyword : str\n    The keyword to validate\n\npos : int, callable\n    If an ``int``, this specifies the exact location this card should\n    have in the header.  Remember that Python is zero-indexed, so this\n    means ", "start_line": 1040, "end_line": 1156, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_datasum", "qualified_name": "add_datasum", "args": ["self", "when", "datasum_keyword"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add the ``DATASUM`` card to this HDU with the value set to the\nchecksum calculated for the data.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwhen : str, optional\n    Comment string for the card that by default represents the\n    time when the checksum was calculated\n\ndatasum_keyword : str, optional\n    The name of the h", "start_line": 1158, "end_line": 1192, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_checksum", "qualified_name": "add_checksum", "args": ["self", "when", "override_datasum", "checksum_keyword", "datasum_keyword"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add the ``CHECKSUM`` and ``DATASUM`` cards to this HDU with\nthe values set to the checksum calculated for the HDU and the\ndata respectively.  The addition of the ``DATASUM`` card may\nbe overridden.\n\nParameters\n----------\nwhen : str, optional\n   comment string for the cards; by default the comments\n ", "start_line": 1194, "end_line": 1247, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "verify_datasum", "qualified_name": "verify_datasum", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Verify that the value in the ``DATASUM`` keyword matches the value\ncalculated for the ``DATASUM`` of the current HDU data.\n\nReturns\n-------\nvalid : int\n   - 0 - failure\n   - 1 - success\n   - 2 - no ``DATASUM`` keyword present", "start_line": 1249, "end_line": 1270, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "verify_checksum", "qualified_name": "verify_checksum", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Verify that the value in the ``CHECKSUM`` keyword matches the\nvalue calculated for the current HDU CHECKSUM.\n\nReturns\n-------\nvalid : int\n   - 0 - failure\n   - 1 - success\n   - 2 - no ``CHECKSUM`` keyword present", "start_line": 1272, "end_line": 1297, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_verify_checksum_datasum", "qualified_name": "_verify_checksum_datasum", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Verify the checksum/datasum values if the cards exist in the header.\nSimply displays warnings if either the checksum or datasum don't match.", "start_line": 1299, "end_line": 1319, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_timestamp", "qualified_name": "_get_timestamp", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the current timestamp in ISO 8601 format, with microseconds\nstripped off.\n\nEx.: 2007-05-30T19:05:11", "start_line": 1321, "end_line": 1329, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"n