 false}, {"name": "info", "qualified_name": "info", "args": ["self", "output"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Summarize the info of the HDUs in this `HDUList`.\n\nNote that this function prints its results to the console---it\ndoes not return a value.\n\nParameters\n----------\noutput : file, bool, optional\n    A file-like object to write the output to.  If `False`, does not\n    output to a file and instead return", "start_line": 912, "end_line": 955, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "filename", "qualified_name": "filename", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the file name associated with the HDUList object if one exists.\nOtherwise returns None.\n\nReturns\n-------\nfilename : a string containing the file name associated with the\n           HDUList object if an association exists.  Otherwise returns\n           None.", "start_line": 957, "end_line": 971, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_readfrom", "qualified_name": "_readfrom", "args": ["cls", "fileobj", "data", "mode", "memmap", "save_backup", "cache", "lazy_load_hdus"], "decorators": ["classmethod"], "docstring": "Provides the implementations from HDUList.fromfile and\nHDUList.fromstring, both of which wrap this method, as their\nimplementations are largely the same.", "start_line": 974, "end_line": 1031, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_try_while_unread_hdus", "qualified_name": "_try_while_unread_hdus", "args": ["self", "func"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Attempt an operation that accesses an HDU by index/name\nthat can fail if not all HDUs have been read yet.  Keep\nreading HDUs until the operation succeeds or there are no\nmore HDUs to read.", "start_line": 1033, "end_line": 1048, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_read_next_hdu", "qualified_name": "_read_next_hdu", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Lazily load a single HDU from the fileobj or data string the `HDUList`\nwas opened from, unless no