": false}, {"name": "is_image", "qualified_name": "is_image", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 186, "end_line": 187, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "section", "qualified_name": "section", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Access a section of the image array without loading the entire array\ninto memory.  The :class:`Section` object returned by this attribute is\nnot meant to be used directly by itself.  Rather, slices of the section\nreturn the appropriate slice of the data, and loads *only* that section\ninto memory.\n\nS", "start_line": 190, "end_line": 204, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "shape", "qualified_name": "shape", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Shape of the image array--should be equivalent to ``self.data.shape``.", "start_line": 207, "end_line": 213, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "header", "qualified_name": "header", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 216, "end_line": 217, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "header", "qualified_name": "header", "args": ["self", "header"], "decorators": ["header.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 220, "end_line": 223, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "data", "qualified_name": "data", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["lazyproperty"], "docstring": "Image/array data as a `~numpy.ndarray`.\n\nPlease remember that the order of axes on an Numpy array are opposite\nof the order specified in the FITS file.  For example for a 2D image\nthe \"rows\" or y-axis are the first dimension, and the \"columns\" or\nx-axis are the second dimension.\n\nIf the data is scal", "start_line": 226, "end_line": 246, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "data", "qualified_name": "data", "args": ["self", "data"], "decorators": ["data.setter"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 249, "end_line": 308, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_header", "qualified_name": "update_header", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the header keywords to agree with the data.", "start_line": 310, "end_line": 375, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update_header_scale_info", "qualified_name": "_update_header_scale_info", "args": ["self", "dtype"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Delete BSCALE/BZERO from header if necessary.", "start_line": 377, "end_line": 428, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "scale", "qualified_name": "scale", "args": ["self", "type", "option", "bscale", "bzero"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Scale image data by using ``BSCALE``/``BZERO``.\n\nCall to this method will scale `data` and update the keywords of\n``BSCALE`` and ``BZERO`` in the HDU's header.  This method should only\nbe used right before writing to the output file, as the data will be\nscaled and is therefore not very usable after ", "start_line": 430, "end_line": 459, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_scale_internal", "qualified_name": "_scale_internal", "args": ["self", "type", "option", "bscale", "bzero", "blank"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "This is an internal implementation of the `scale` method, which\nalso supports handling BLANK properly.\n\nTODO: This is only needed for fixing #3865 without introducing any\npublic API changes.  We should support BLANK better when rescaling\ndata, and when that is added the need for this internal interf", "start_line": 461, "end_line": 564, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_verify", "qualified_name": "_verify", "args": ["self", "option"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 566, "end_line": 572, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_verify_blank", "qualified_name": "_verify_blank", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 574, "end_line": 598, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_prewriteto", "qu