g", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "testConstructorNameArg\n\nPassing name='...' to the BinTableHDU and TableHDU constructors\nshould set the .name attribute and 'EXTNAME' header keyword, and\noverride any name in an existing 'EXTNAME' value.", "start_line": 1495, "end_line": 1522, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_constructor_ver_arg", "qualified_name": "test_constructor_ver_arg", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1524, "end_line": 1544, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_unicode_colname", "qualified_name": "test_unicode_colname", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/issues/5204\n\"Handle unicode FITS BinTable column names on Python 2\"", "start_line": 1546, "end_line": 1553, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_bin_table_with_logical_array", "qualified_name": "test_bin_table_with_logical_array", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1555, "end_line": 1572, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_fits_rec_column_access", "qualified_name": "test_fits_rec_column_access", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1574, "end_line": 1580, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_with_zero_width_column", "qualified_name": "test_table_with_zero_width_column", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1582, "end_line": 1627, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_string_column_padding", "qualified_name": "test_string_column_padding", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1629, "end_line": 1662, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_multi_dimensional_columns", "qualified_name": "test_multi_dimensional_columns", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests the multidimensional column implementation with both numeric\narrays and string arrays.", "start_line": 1664, "end_line": 1727, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_bin_table_init_from_string_array_column", "qualified_name": "test_bin_table_init_from_string_array_column", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests two ways of creating a new `BinTableHDU` from a column of\nstring arrays.\n\nThis tests for a couple different regressions, and ensures that\nboth BinTableHDU(data=arr) and BinTableHDU.from_columns(arr) work\nequivalently.\n\nSome of this is redundant with the following test, but checks some\nsubtly d", "start_line": 1729, "end_line": 1770, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_columns_with_truncating_tdim", "qualified_name": "test_columns_with_truncating_tdim", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "According to the FITS standard (section 7.3.2):\n\n    If the number of elements in the array implied by the TDIMn is less\n    than the allocated size of the ar- ray in the FITS file, then the\n    unused trailing elements should be interpreted as containing\n    undefined fill values.\n\n*deep sigh* What", "start_line": 1772, "end_line": 1816, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_string_array_round_trip", "qualified_name": "test_string_array_round_trip", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/201", "start_line": 1818, "end_line": 1850, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_new_table_with_nd_column", "qualified_name": "test_new_table_with_nd_column", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for\nhttps://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/3", "start_line": 1852, "end_line": 1877, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_mismatched_tform_and_tdim", "qualified_name": "test_mismatched_tform_and_tdim", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Normally the product of the dimensions listed in a TDIMn keyword\nmust be less than or equal to the repeat count in the TFORMn keyword.\n\nThis tests that this works if less than (treating the trailing bytes\nas unspecified fill values per the FITS standard) and fails if the\ndimensions specified by TDIM", "start_line": 1879, "end_line": 1911, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_tdim_of_size_one", "qualified_name": "test_tdim_of_size_one", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/astropy/astropy/pull/3580", "start_line": 1913, "end_line": 1917, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_slicing", "qualified_name": "test_slicing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/52", "start_line": 1919, "end_line": 1935, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_slicing", "qualified_name": "test_array_slicing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/55", "start_line": 1937, "end_line": 1951, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_broadcasting", "qualified_name": "test_array_broadcasting", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/pull/48", "start_line": 1953, "end_line": 1968, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_array_slicing_readonly", "qualified_name": "test_array_slicing_readonly", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Like test_array_slicing but with the file opened in 'readonly' mode.\nRegression test for a crash when slicing readonly memmap'd tables.", "start_line": 1970, "end_line": 1986, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_dump_load_round_trip", "qualified_name": "test_dump_load_round_trip", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A simple test of the dump/load methods; dump the data, column, and\nheader files and try to reload the table from them.", "start_line": 1988, "end_line": 2007, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_dump_load_array_colums", "qualified_name": "test_dump_load_array_colums", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://github.com/spacetelescope/PyFITS/issues/22\n\nEnsures that a table containing a multi-value array column can be\ndumped and loaded successfully.", "start_line": 2009, "end_line": 2028, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_load_guess_format", "qualified_name": "test_load_guess_format", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Tests loading a table dump with no supplied coldefs or header, so that\nthe table format has to be guessed at.  There is of course no exact\nscience to this; the table that's produced simply uses sensible guesses\nfor that format.  Ideally this should never have to be used.", "start_line": 2030, "end_line": 2070, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_attribute_field_shadowing", "qualified_name": "test_attribute_field_shadowing", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/86\n\nNumpy recarray objects have a poorly-considered feature of allowing\nfield access by attribute lookup.  However, if a field name conincides\nwith an existing attribute/method of the array, the existing name takes\nprecence (making th", "start_line": 2072, "end_line": 2095, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_from_bool_fields", "qualified_name": "test_table_from_bool_fields", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Regression test for https://aeon.stsci.edu/ssb/trac/pyfits/ticket/113\n\nTests creating a table from a recarray containing numpy.bool columns.", "start_line": 2097, "end_line": 2113, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_table_from_bool_fields2", "qualified_name": "test_table_from_bool_fields2", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstrin